window.L5R_CHARACTER = {"slug":"nasu-kogo","name":"Nasu Kogo","clan":"Phoenix","family":"Nasu","school":"Shosuro Shadowweaver School","role":"Shugenja","bucket":"Shugenja","campaign":"The Bushi Oni","accent":"#5b398e","portrait":"src/portraits/nasu-kogo.png","concept":null,"summary":null,"tier_count":4,"xp_min":0,"xp_max":63,"twenty_questions":{"template":"core","generated":true,"steps":{"step1":{"answers":{"clan":"Phoenix","ring":"void","skill":"theology","social_status":30},"picks":{}},"step2":{"answers":{"family":"Nasu (Shiba Vassal)","ring":"water","skill1":"meditation","skill2":"tactics","wealth":5,"social_glory":40},"picks":{}},"step3":{"answers":{"school":"Shoshuro Shadoweaver School","roles":"Shugenja","ring1":"air","ring2":"fire","skill1":"courtesy","skill2":"government","skill3":"skulduggery","social_honor":30},"picks":{"techniques":["Prey on the Weak","Commune with the Spirits","By the Light of the Lord Moon","Cloak of Night","Fukurokujin’s Wit"],"school_ability":["Sudden Nightfall"],"equipment":["Concealed Armor","Sanctified Robes","Wakizashi","Shuriken","Poison (One Vial)","Tetsubishi"]}},"step4":{"answers":{"stand_out":"Kogo is experimental and creative in her work.","ring":"fire"},"picks":{}},"step5":{"answers":{"social_giri":"Her lord is Nasu Tadaaki, her own father and current head of the declining Nasu family. Her duty is to restore the family's status and influence with the Imperial families. Kogo must prove the Nasu worthy of their former position."},"picks":{}},"step6":{"answers":{"social_ninjo":"Kogo yearns for power that cannot be taken away by political whims or clan hierarchies. Deep down, she wants to transcend the petty limitations of clan politics entirely - to become something more than a samurai bound by duty and status."},"picks":{}},"step7":{"answers":{"clan_relations":"Publicly, Kogo is a dutiful daughter of the Phoenix, respectful of tradition and the Elemental Council. Privately, she seethes at how the clan's rigid hierarchies and spiritual purity have constrained her family's potential. She sees the Phoenix as hidebound, more concerned with ancient texts than real power, more worried about propriety than results.","skill":"sentiment","social_add_glory":0},"picks":{}},"step8":{"answers":{"bushido":"Kogo believes that the ends justify the means. Bushido matters mostly as a matter of what is observed; what is unobserved is not beholden.","skill":"skulduggery","social_add_honor":0,"tenet_paramount":" Duty and Loyalty","tenet_less_significant":"Compassion"},"picks":{}},"step9":{"answers":{"success":"During her final year at the Shosuro Shadowweaver School, Kogo uncovered a Lion Clan conspiracy against Scorpion trade interests in the capital. Rather than simply reporting it to her sensei, she manipulated the situation—feeding the conspirators false information while ensuring the Scorpion's countermove appeared as superior planning rather than intelligence work. In the process, she obtained compromising evidence against Akodo Nobuhiko, a Lion courtier stationed at Otosan Uchi, which she quietly kept for herself."},"picks":{"distinction":["Blackmail on [Name]"]}},"step10":{"answers":{"difficulty":"During her Scorpion training, Kogo discovered a hidden scroll tucked away in her sensei's private collection—a fragmentary document on forbidden techniques that she believes the Scorpion was saving for leverage. She copied it in secret, certain she was the first to read it in years, and the text spoke of power beyond the kami's limitations. The knowledge was intoxicating, and when she attempted the first technique described within, she succeeded—but something dark answered her call. She gained power, but also corruption she can never fully cleanse. The Shadowlands Taint now marks her spiritual essence, a constant reminder that she has stepped onto a path from which there may be no return."},"picks":{"adversity":["Shadowlands Taint (Air)"]}},"step11":{"answers":{"calms":"Despite her ambitions and resentments, Kogo finds genuine tranquility in the traditional tea ceremony. In those quiet, ritualized moments—the precise movements, the meditative focus, the temporary suspension of scheming and striving—she can almost forget her burdens."},"picks":{"passion":["Tea"]}},"step12":{"answers":{"worries":"Kogo lives in constant fear that her maho practice will be discovered before she achieves her goals, which would mean execution and her family's destruction. Worse still, she has become convinced that conspiracies surround her—that rival Phoenix families work to keep the Nasu marginalized, that the Scorpion suspect what she stole, that someone is always watching and waiting for her to slip. She sees patterns and plots in innocent coincidences, reads threat into casual questions, and trusts almost no one. Whether these conspiracies are real or products of her guilty conscience hardly matters; the paranoia shapes every decision she makes."},"picks":{"anxiety":["Conspiracy"]}},"step13":{"answers":{"most_learn":"Shiba Atsutane was assigned as Kogo's sponsor when she first arrived at Otosan Uchi—a well-meaning Phoenix courtier who was supposed to guide her entry into Imperial politics. Instead, she watched him destroy his own career within six months. Atsutane's fatal flaw was that he actually cared about the people affected by court decisions; he advocated too openly for the suffering, showed too much genuine emotion, and completely failed to read when powerful figures wanted problems ignored rather than solved. His compassion made him predictable, exploitable, and ultimately disposable. When he was quietly recalled to Phoenix lands in disgrace, Kogo stepped smoothly into his position—having learned that court is performance, that sincerity is a liability, and that compassion is a luxury for those who can afford to lose. She feels no sympathy for his fall; he had it coming, and she's more than happy to replace him.","skill":"performance"},"picks":{"disadvantage":["Disdain for Compassion"]}},"step14":{"answers":{"first_sight":"Where many would have their own scribes, she takes her own copious notes at all times, in an elegant personal cipher."},"picks":{"special_features":["Calligraphy Set"]}},"step15":{"answers":{"stress":"She organizes her spaces, demanding a complete sense of control over her environment."},"picks":{}},"step16":{"answers":{"relations":"Kogo maintains a careful relationship with Bayushi Toshiro, a mid-ranking Scorpion operative in Otosan Uchi who served as one of her instructors. He occasionally feeds her intelligence about court intrigues—partly because the Scorpion value having a Phoenix ally, partly because he enjoys keeping her in his debt.\n\nKogo has cultivated a relationship with the proprietress of the Plum Blossom Tea House, a neutral meeting ground for courtiers in Otosan Uchi. The woman, Usagi Hanako (a Hare Clan vassal family member), runs the establishment as a place where \"all are welcome to find peace\"—but she's also remarkably well-informed about court gossip and has helped Kogo navigate the capital's social waters."},"picks":{"item":["Personal Seal or Chop"]}},"step17":{"answers":{"parents_pov":"To Nasu Tadaaki, Kogo is \"the future of our family, the one who will reclaim our rightful place.\" He describes her with a mixture of pride and barely concealed desperation—she is his only child, his last chance to restore the Nasu name before he dies. He speaks of her accomplishments with fierce pride to anyone who will listen, perhaps too loudly, too insistently, as if he can will the world to recognize her worth through sheer force of repetition. Other nobles find his advocacy unseemly; Kogo finds it suffocating. The weight of being everything to him is crushing.","skill":"composition"},"picks":{}},"step18":{"answers":{"heritage_name":"Kogo was named after her aunt, Nasu Kogo the Elder, a talented performer and courtier who was considered the family's brightest star a generation ago. Two years ago, Aunt Kogo was invited to perform in an imperial theatrical production—a tremendous honor and exactly the kind of recognition the Nasu desperately needed. Instead, she delivered a catastrophically bad performance. Whether from nerves, illness, or simple misfortune, she forgot lines, missed cues, and finally froze entirely on stage. The Emperor himself left the theater in discomfort. The shame was so profound that Aunt Kogo took the tonsure and entered a monastery, but the damage was done—rumors spread that the Nasu family is cursed by Benten-no-kami for some forgotten slight against the arts. Young Kogo now carries not just her aunt's name, but the burden of redeeming it.","heritage_1":4,"heritage_2":9,"heritage_add_honor":0,"heritage_add_glory":0,"heritage_add_status":-3,"skill":"command"},"picks":{"heritage_item":["Benten’s Curse"]}},"step19":{"answers":{"firstname":"Kogo"},"picks":{}},"step20":{"answers":{"death":"When the Nasu name has finally been restored to its rightful place among the Phoenix—when her father has seen his family honored once more, when the whispers of curses have been replaced with respect, when she has proven that will and ability matter more than bloodline—then and only then should Kogo die. She imagines herself at the pinnacle of her power, having mastered both legitimate magic and the forbidden arts, having achieved everything she set out to accomplish. In that moment of triumph, she would take her own life in a final act of control, silencing the kansen that whisper in her mind, severing the corruption before it can spread to others or taint her family's restored glory."},"picks":{}}}},"notes":"","curriculum":[{"rank":1,"kind":"Skill Group","group":null,"label":"Social Skills","prereq":false},{"rank":1,"kind":"Skill","group":null,"label":"Fitness","prereq":false},{"rank":1,"kind":"Skill","group":null,"label":"Government","prereq":false},{"rank":1,"kind":"Skill","group":null,"label":"Martial Arts [Ranged]","prereq":false},{"rank":1,"kind":"Tech. Grp.","group":"shuji","label":"Rank 1 Shuji","prereq":true},{"rank":1,"kind":"Technique","group":"ninjutsu","label":"Skulk","prereq":true},{"rank":1,"kind":"Technique","group":"ninjutsu","label":"Deadly Sting","prereq":true},{"rank":2,"kind":"Skill Group","group":null,"label":"Scholar Skills","prereq":false},{"rank":2,"kind":"Skill","group":null,"label":"Courtesy","prereq":false},{"rank":2,"kind":"Skill","group":null,"label":"Martial Arts [Ranged]","prereq":false},{"rank":2,"kind":"Skill","group":null,"label":"Skulduggery","prereq":false},{"rank":2,"kind":"Tech. Grp.","group":"invocation","label":"Rank 1-2 Invocations","prereq":false},{"rank":2,"kind":"Technique","group":"invocation","label":"Fluid Shadows","prereq":false},{"rank":2,"kind":"Technique","group":"shuji","label":"Lord Bayushi’s Whispers (Scorpion)","prereq":true},{"rank":3,"kind":"Skill Group","group":null,"label":"Martial Skills","prereq":false},{"rank":3,"kind":"Skill","group":null,"label":"Government","prereq":false},{"rank":3,"kind":"Skill","group":null,"label":"Sentiment","prereq":false},{"rank":3,"kind":"Skill","group":null,"label":"Skulduggery","prereq":false},{"rank":3,"kind":"Tech. Grp.","group":"shuji","label":"Rank 1-3 Shuji","prereq":true},{"rank":3,"kind":"Technique","group":"invocation","label":"Dream Painter","prereq":false},{"rank":3,"kind":"Technique","group":"ninjutsu","label":"Noxious Cloud","prereq":true},{"rank":4,"kind":"Skill Group","group":null,"label":"Social Skills","prereq":false},{"rank":4,"kind":"Skill","group":null,"label":"Culture","prereq":false},{"rank":4,"kind":"Skill","group":null,"label":"Martial Arts [Ranged]","prereq":false},{"rank":4,"kind":"Skill","group":null,"label":"Theology","prereq":false},{"rank":4,"kind":"Tech. Grp.","group":"invocation","label":"Rank 1-4 Invocations","prereq":false},{"rank":4,"kind":"Technique","group":"shuji","label":"Wolf’s Proposal","prereq":true},{"rank":4,"kind":"Technique","group":"kata","label":"Pin the Fan","prereq":true},{"rank":5,"kind":"Skill Group","group":null,"label":"Martial Skills","prereq":false},{"rank":5,"kind":"Skill","group":null,"label":"Culture","prereq":false},{"rank":5,"kind":"Skill","group":null,"label":"Medicine","prereq":false},{"rank":5,"kind":"Skill","group":null,"label":"Skulduggery","prereq":false},{"rank":5,"kind":"Tech. Grp.","group":"shuji","label":"Rank 1-5 Shuji","prereq":true},{"rank":5,"kind":"Technique","group":"invocation","label":"The Fading Dream","prereq":false},{"rank":5,"kind":"Technique","group":"ninjutsu","label":"Silencing Stroke","prereq":true}],"tiers":[{"xp":0,"label":null,"rank":1,"school":"Shosuro Shadowweaver School","foundry_id":"1couuYrLcG6efybt","rings":{"air":2,"earth":1,"fire":3,"water":2,"void":2},"skills":{"artisan":{"aesthetics":0,"composition":1,"design":0,"smithing":0},"martial":{"fitness":0,"melee":0,"ranged":0,"unarmed":0,"meditation":1,"tactics":1},"scholar":{"culture":0,"government":1,"medicine":0,"sentiment":1,"theology":1},"social":{"command":1,"courtesy":1,"games":0,"performance":1},"trade":{"commerce":0,"labor":0,"seafaring":0,"skulduggery":2,"survival":0}},"social":{"honor":30,"glory":40,"status":27,"ninjo":"Kogo yearns for power that cannot be taken away by political whims or clan hierarchies. Deep down, she wants to transcend the petty limitations of clan politics entirely - to become something more than a samurai bound by duty and status.","giri":"Her lord is Nasu Tadaaki, her own father and current head of the declining Nasu family. Her duty is to restore the family's status and influence with the Imperial families. Kogo must prove the Nasu worthy of their former position.","bushido_tenets":{"paramount":" Duty and Loyalty","less_significant":"Compassion"}},"derived":{"endurance":8,"composure":6,"focus":5,"vigilance":2,"void_points":2},"money":{"zeni":0,"koku":0,"bu":0},"advancements":[],"techniques":[{"name":"Prey on the Weak","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"shuji","rank":2,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Court is not a kind place, and a harsh word is no less cruel for being spoken softly and with perfect etiquette.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">As a Scheme action, you may make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">TN 1 Courtesy (air) check </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">targeting a Compromised character.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, your target must choose one of the following:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">- Immediately unmask in a manner of their choosing based on the circumstances.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">- Forfeit glory equal to your Air Ring plus your bonus successes to leave the scene.</span></p></li></ul><h4><span class=\"fontstyle5\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(air)</span><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle7\">+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If the target chooses to unmask, you learn one of their disadvantages of their choice per (op) spent this way.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(air)</span><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle7\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If the target chooses to leave the scene, you notice their destination from the direction of their departure or overhear from the crowd where they will retreat.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":215},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-shuji-l5r-sortilege.Item.ekziVajOr3Up1EjP","skill":"courtesy"},{"name":"Commune with the Spirits","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"ritual","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>The ritualist centers their mind on one of the Elements, appealing to the spirits in their environment and seeking their counsel or boon. Priests and laypeople are able to use this ritual to receive less specific guidance from the spirits, such as a leaf that falls to the ground pointing in the direction of the person or thing they are seeking.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">As a downtime activity or Support action, you may make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">TN 1 Theology check </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">using (air), (earth), (fire), (water), or (void) to appeal to nearby spirits of that Element (appeal to the departed, such as ancestor spirits, and other non-elemental supernatural presences, if using (void)) for aid.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, choose and receive one of the following boons from the spirit or spirits you contacted:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- Sense the Kami: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Detect all spirits and uses of their magic by shugenja within a number of range bands equal to the ring you used plus your bonus successes.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- Spiritual Knowledge: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Learn one fact the spirits know about the area.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- Elemental Gift: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">The kami deliver a small amount of the Element in question to you. For instance, a prayer to a water kami might cause it to begin raining lightly, for a short time, but it might also cause you to run across a stream, or even find groundwater. In contrast, a prayer to fire kami might bring forth a small shower of sparks, while a prayer to an air kami might elicit a gust of wind. Praying to an earth kami might cause you to stumble across a large stone, or find a small patch of arable ground amid a wasteland. Prayers to the ancestors may allow the petitioner to find something that belonged to an ancestor in a time of need.</span></p></li></ul><h4><span class=\"fontstyle5\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Reduce the TN of your next check to interact with or appeal to kami or supernatural presences of this Element by 1.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, receive one additional boon per </span><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op) </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">spent this way. Each boon can only be received one time per activation.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":212},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-rituals-l5r-sortilege.Item.r9DyFb62vtLwexbW","skill":"theology"},{"name":"By the Light of the Lord Moon","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"invocation","rank":1,"description":"<p>Kitsuki's Eyes (Ancestral), Wind Scatters Shadow (Elemental), Reveal the World of Ghosts (Foreign)</p><p><em>When a shugenja performs this invocation, the light shifts to that of a moonlit night, unweaving the shadows to lay bare the things they conceal. Hidden objects glow faintly with silver light, while mystical illusions are revealed as translucent, gossamer forms.</em></p><p><strong>Activation:</strong> As a Scheme action, you may make a TN 2 Theology (air) check targeting an area at range 0–2 of you.</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> If you succeed, you scry for each hidden character and concealed object (such as secret compartments, trap doors, and concealed weapons) in the targeted area, revealing it with an illusory, luminous outline that only you can perceive. This invocation only reveals objects and people concealed by mundane means.</p><h4>New Opportunities</h4><p>(air)(op)+: If you succeed, you may also reveal up to one magically concealed object per (op) spent this way.</p><p>Air(op)(op)+: Choose one additional character at range 0–1 per (op)(op) spent this way. The chosen characters can also see the objects.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":192},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-invocations-l5r-sortilege.Item.X37l2OFmdoUXYJtX","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Cloak of Night","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"invocation","rank":1,"description":"<p>Smoke of Stolen Light (Alchemy), Shroud of the North Wind (Fortunist), Walk in the Shadow World (Foreign)</p><p><em>A sufficiently learned shugenja can call forth air kami to play one of their simplest and most effective tricks: enveloping an object or person in their embrace to hide it from sight.</em></p><p><strong>Activation:</strong> As a Scheme and Support action, you may make a Theology (air) check targeting one object or character at range 0–1. The TN is equal to the target’s silhouette (see page 265).</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> If you succeed, you augment the target with an illusion that renders it invisible to the naked eye. The object is still physically present and can be touched, smelled, or sensed with any normal sense other than vision. This effect persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to your bonus successes.</p><h4>New Opportunities</h4><p>(air)(op)(op)+: Choose one additional target of the same silhouette or smaller per (op)(op) spent this way.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":192},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-invocations-l5r-sortilege.Item.fveOrp1xJ9uGnNCl","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Fukurokujin’s Wit","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"invocation","rank":1,"description":"<p>Wisdom of the Kitsu (Ancestral), Ignite the Mind's Candle (Elemental), Mantra of the Scholar Kings (Foreign)</p><p><em>Shujenja are scholars at their heart, for their art is one of long hours of study and dedication to the refinement of the mind. Thus, many seek the blessing of Fukurokujin, keeper of knowledge and patron to scholars. A shugenja can call upon the guidance of this Fortune to sharpen their mind to a razor edge and vitalize their nerves.</em></p><p><strong>Activation:</strong> As a Support action, you may make a TN 1 Theology (fire) check targeting yourself.</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> If you succeed, you augment your target’s wits and cunning with the Fortune’s favor. When making checks, the target adds a kept (ring) set to an (op)(st) result. This effect persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to your bonus successes.</p><h4>New Opportunities</h4><p>(fire)(op): You may target another character at range 0–2 instead of yourself.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":203},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-invocations-l5r-sortilege.Item.bH76OcZ5FOcuLRXx","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Sudden Nightfall","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":0,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"school_ability","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">You do not suffer any ill effects of Obscuring terrain as a result of darkness (see page 267 of the core rulebook). When you perform an Attack or Scheme action check against a target in terrain that is Obscuring due to darkness, reduce the TN by your school rank (to a minimum of 1).</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">As a Support action, you may target a position at range 0–2 and </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">summon </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">a cloud of supernatural darkness there. An area around the target position extending a number of range bands equal to your Air Ring become Obscuring terrain. This effect persists a number of rounds equal to your school rank.</span></p>","source":{"book":"celestial_realms","page":87},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.school-abilities-l5r-sortilege.Item.a06K6G42WcqlCnxQ"}],"peculiarities":[{"name":"Blackmail on Akodo Nobuhiko","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"distinction","ring":"fire","types":"Interpersonal","custom":true,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>“I had hoped to find you here,” Yogo Hiroue began. “It has been too long since we last spoke plainly.”</em></span></p><p></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">The following apply to a character with the Blackmail on [Name] distinction:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">- You have incriminating information on an individual, which you use to force them to help you even when doing so may damage their reputation. They will share what knowledge they have about a given person, item, location, or situation, whether through a face-to-face meeting or through written correspondence. They will also arrange for introductions with exclusive members of society or places of business. Confer with the GM to select a campaign-appropriate NPC when choosing this advantage.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">- When performing a check to demand favors of the chosen individual (such as a Courtesy (fire) check to remind them of the consequences of their disobeying you or a Command (fire) check to order them to risk themself on your behalf), you may reroll up to two dice.</span></p></li></ul>","source_reference":{"source":"core_rulebook","page":102}},{"name":"Tea","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"passion","ring":"void","types":"Physical, Spiritual","description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>“Without the bastions of civility that are teahouses, the Empire would surely collapse into chaos.”</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><em>– Kakita Yoshi, Daimyō of the Kakita Family</em></span></p><p></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">The following apply to a character with the Tea passion:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- You can identify regional variations in tea, and you know a great deal about the process of preparing and drying leaves. In the wilderness, you can acquire the natural ingredients required to make rustic teas of various sorts with relative ease.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- After performing a check to interact with tea (such as a Medicine (void) check to brew a tea with ingredients that help the body recover from illness or a Performance (void) check to perform a tea ceremony that helps the recipients contemplate their state in life), you remove 3 strife.</span></p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":115},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.passions-l5r-sortilege.Item.wiz5rooMR3tqtULe"},{"name":"Shadowlands Taint (Air)","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"adversity","ring":"air","types":"Curse, Interpersonal, Spiritual","description":"<p><em>The Obsidian Journal is a secret text, written hundreds  of years ago by Kuni Shunsuke, a Crab Clan samurai who made forbidden journeys into the Shadowlands  and wrote of what he saw there.</em></p><p><em>By the end of his journal, he wrote: “Even now, I know that the fingers of shadow have reached too deeply within me, for although I am surrounded by family and clan, I feel no kinship. They seem distant to me, as if viewed through a glass. I wonder how much of myself is truly left.”</em></p><p><em>That was the final entry of the Obsidian Journal. Kuni Shunsuke committed seppuku to silence the call of the Shadowlands.</em></p><p></p><p>The following apply to a character with the Shadowlands Taint (Air) adversity:</p><ul><li><p>-  You are a Tainted being. You have trouble sympathizing with other humans, but you can understand the emotions of corrupted beings easily.</p></li><li><p>-  When you make a check to show compassion for other human beings (such as a Composition (air) check to edit a work for emotional refinement or a Courtesy (air) check to say something difficult without harming the recipient’s feelings), you must choose and reroll two dice containing (su) or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point.</p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":127},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.adversities-l5r-sortilege.Item.eEg9b6rmnSBA5HqG"},{"name":"Conspiracy","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"anxiety","ring":"earth","types":"Interpersonal, Mental","description":"<p><em>“Why is she never seen out during the day?”</em></p><p><em>“Genjirō, you know the family keeps Lady Kaguya out of the sun because she burns so easily.”</em></p><p><em>“No, it’s because she feeds off the light of the moon.”</em></p><p><em>His friend sighed. “Moon people don’t exist, you know.”</em></p><p><em>“They do! They eat the dreams of their lovers, causing terrible nightmares.”</em></p><p><em>“Wait, does she eat dreams or moonlight?”</em></p><p><em>“You aren’t listening! If our lady’s bride-to-be isn’t human, we have to warn her. Now, moon people have a crescent-shaped birthmark on their—”</em></p><p><em>“We are not sneaking into Lady Kaguya’s bedroom to search her body! Do you want your head chopped off?”</em></p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> The following apply to a character with the Conspiracy anxiety:</p><ul><li><p>- You are plagued by the knowledge that there are greater plots in the world than what most others can see. Everywhere, treacherous schemes wait to ruin the lives of good people, and you cannot help but warn others of these awful machinations.</p></li><li><p>- After performing a check to interact with an unfamiliar authority figure (such as a Courtesy (earth) check to be properly deferential or a Government (earth) check to remember an authority figure’s specific role), you receive 3 strife. If this is the first time this has occurred this scene, gain 1 Void point.</p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"celestial_realms","page":91},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.anxieties-l5r-sortilege.Item.wBeHgMqK2BL7fX6I"},{"name":"Disdain for Compassion","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"adversity","ring":"water","types":"Flaw, Mental","description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>“We Brothers of the Boar are very loyal samurai, indeed! Loyal to money, loyal to our bellies, loyal to ourselves, and what higher virtue could there be, brothers, eh?”</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><em>- The Rōnin Kujira</em></span></p><p></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">The following apply to a character with the Disdain for Compassion adversity:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- You no longer believe in the tenet of Compassion, though you still lose honor for disobeying it. When you act in accordance with this tenet of Bushidō, others can sometimes sense your insincerity.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- When you make a check to pay lip service to this tenet of Bushidō or to uphold it (such as a Courtesy check to express its importance or a Meditation check to use a belief in this tenet to your advantage), you must choose and reroll two dice containing </span><span class=\"fontstyle5\">(su) </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point.</span></p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":120},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.adversities-l5r-sortilege.Item.WLiIHkS6o7pS2u9y"},{"name":"Benten’s Curse","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"adversity","ring":"air","types":"Interpersonal, Spiritual","description":"<p><em>One of the more popular tales of the rakugoka, the professional storytellers of Rokugan, is that of the Artless Artist. A comedic tale, it is the story of a court artist who was utterly lacking in any genuine talent and had such an unpleasant demeanor that nobody would ever love him. The telling of the tale varies from performance to performance, with the rakugoka spinning unique and outrageous recountings of the artist’s misadventures tailored to the tastes of their particular audience.</em></p><p></p><p>The following apply to a character with the Benten’s Curse adversity:</p><ul><li><p>- Your romantic efforts are always stymied by circumstances, and your gestures to get the romantic attention of others are usually misinterpreted.</p></li><li><p>- When you make a check to express your admiration to someone (such as an Aesthetics (air) check to find the right poem to read to express your feelings or a Courtesy (air) check to tell someone your feelings without exceeding propriety), you must choose and reroll two dice containing (su) or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point.</p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":116},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.adversities-l5r-sortilege.Item.wx0TwgTwrxGMVd1g"}],"titles":[],"bonds":[],"gear":[{"name":"Wakizashi","quantity":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Whereas the katana represents a samurai’s status as a warrior, the wakizashi represents their place in Rokugan’s social order and strict caste system. The wakizashi is a small, katana-like sword usually two to three feet in length, with the same flexible blade and lethal edge. It is often made as part of a pair, with the same decorations as its matched katana. The wakizashi also fills another role: it clearly signals that its wearer is a samurai, and a person of honor who will make the ultimate sacrifice for their ideals and their master. It is the tool with which a samurai commits seppuku: ritual suicide, the last protest of an aggrieved and honorable samurai.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":233},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.weapons-l5r-sortilege.Item.S1MG4qPHEV3N8XnO","damage":3,"deadliness":5,"range":"0-1","grip_2":"Deadliness +2","skill":"melee","category":"Swords","rarity":"7","zeni":"15 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000002","name":"Ceremonial"},{"id":"L5RCorePro000001","name":"Razor-Edged"}]},{"name":"Shuriken","quantity":6,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Favored by shinobi, shuriken are small metal discs with a sharpened edge that come in a dizzying array of sizes and styles. They are designed mainly to distract, but shuriken can also be coated with toxins for lethality, and any cutting edge can kill if used properly.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":237},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.weapons-l5r-sortilege.Item.5Lr1CNs1uvX7J38y","damage":2,"deadliness":4,"range":"0","grip_1":"(stab or slash): -, (thrown): Martial Arts [Ranged], Range 1-3","grip_2":"N/A","skill":"unarmed","category":"Specialist Weapons","rarity":"6","zeni":"1 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000005","name":"Concealable"}]},{"name":"Concealed Armor","quantity":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Used by cautious courtiers, shinobi, and anyone else who fears assassination, concealed armor is a kimono, keikogi, or other garment with thin bamboo or metal plates sewn inside to turn an unexpected blade or arrow.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":239},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.armors-l5r-sortilege.Item.vDEAuVf0o5GwmVsB","armor":{"physical":2,"supernatural":0},"rarity":"4","zeni":"5 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000005","name":"Concealable"}]},{"name":"Sanctified Robes","quantity":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">The vestments of shugenja, shrine keepers, and other religious figures are blessed by kami and thus grant mystical protection. Traditionally, such robes consist of a white garment called </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">jōe </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">(literally, “pure cloth”) and a peaked hat, but they can be simpler, such as a white haori top and red hakama bottoms, or even an elaborate kimono.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":239},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.armors-l5r-sortilege.Item.Cq1koK56k9dvLfMh","armor":{"physical":1,"supernatural":3},"rarity":"7","zeni":"4 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000002","name":"Ceremonial"}]},{"name":"Poison (One Vial)","quantity":3,"description":"<p>In the courts of the Emerald Empire, the wheels of politics are sometimes turned by unsavory means. Members of the Scorpion Clan are certainly not above using poison to weaken or eliminate political rivals—not that one could ever prove their culpability—and many samurai turn to such measures in times of desperation or fear. (Cost: 30 zeni for one dose. Rarity: 5. Qualities: Forbidden.)</p><p data-start=\"482\" data-end=\"1061\">Three poisons found in Rokugan are:<br data-start=\"517\" data-end=\"520\">$ Noxious Poison: A catchall term for a wide variety of deadly compounds (many of which have perfectly legitimate uses in medicine and other trades), these sorts of poisons often act by attacking the heart, organs, or brain directly.<br data-start=\"753\" data-end=\"756\">– When a character ingests noxious poison, the character suffers a critical strike with severity 10. The poisoner may spend  on their check to deliver the poison to increase the severity by 1 per  spent this way.<br data-start=\"970\" data-end=\"973\">– When noxious poison is applied to a weapon, increase that weapon’s deadliness by +4.</p><p data-start=\"1063\" data-end=\"1509\">$ Fire Biter: A poison that wracks victims with searing pain, fire biter is easily identified by its bitter taste, which makes it difficult to disguise its presence in food or drink.<br data-start=\"1245\" data-end=\"1248\">– When a character ingests fire biter, the character suffers 5 strife and the Dazed and Exhausted conditions.<br data-start=\"1357\" data-end=\"1360\">– When fire biter is applied to a weapon, after a target suffers a critical strike from the weapon, they suffer the Dazed and Exhausted conditions.</p><p data-start=\"1511\" data-end=\"1962\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">$ Night Milk: A favorite of the Shosuro family, night milk is a dizzying concoction that must be injected or otherwise delivered directly into the bloodstream.<br data-start=\"1670\" data-end=\"1673\">– When night milk is introduced into a character’s bloodstream, the character suffers 5 fatigue and the Disoriented and Prone conditions.<br data-start=\"1810\" data-end=\"1813\">– When night milk is applied to a weapon, after a target suffers a critical strike from the weapon, they suffer the Disoriented and Prone conditions.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":244},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.SNTCLZ2aScPEddId","rarity":"5","zeni":"30 zeni","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000009","name":"Forbidden"}]},{"name":"Tetsubishi","quantity":1,"description":"<p>A type of caltrop welded together in the shape of sharp-spined stars the size of a fist or larger, tetsubishi are a type of iron makibishi designed to be scattered on the battlefield in front of fortifications as a defense. They may also be used to delay pursuers. While their sharp edges may pierce the soles of unsuspecting samurai’s boots, these mass-produced weapons are especially effective at penetrating the hooves of horses used by cavalry and mounted infantry.</p><p data-start=\"473\" data-end=\"732\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">As an Attack and Support action, a character may scatter a handful of tetsubishi targeting a patch of ground at range 0–2. The terrain at range 0–1 from the point of impact gains the Dangerous and Ensnaring terrain quality. (Cost: 5 bu per handful. Rarity: 4)</p>","source":{"book":"fields_of_victory","page":91},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.4OCDJyLlEF5F7feH","rarity":"4","zeni":"5 bu"},{"name":"Calligraphy Set","quantity":1,"description":"<p>These ornate boxes contain items a practiced calligrapher needs to craft books, letters, scrolls, and other written communications. It consists of a small wooden box that contains a variety of brushes, inkstones, and pigments; a small bowl for water; and a small bag of sand for drying. Calligraphers and scribes customarily carry a calligraphy set, as so do some samurai and courtiers who prefer to write their own correspondence. (Cost: 1 bu. Rarity: 3.)</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":242},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.MWzx5Wiu6xcCWc9J","rarity":"3","zeni":"1 bu"},{"name":"Personal Seal or Chop","quantity":1,"description":"<p>A personal chop is used by samurai to verify their identity and sign documents, among other official business. Each one is a unique design that is registered with the Miya family. Using another samurai’s chop is considered both an insult and a serious crime. (Cost: 4 bu. Rarity: 6. Qualities: Ceremonial.)</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":243},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.UU5eQKPBQZ9ilOTF","rarity":"6","zeni":"4 bu","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000002","name":"Ceremonial"}]}]},{"xp":20,"label":"Rank 2","rank":2,"school":"Shosuro Shadowweaver School","foundry_id":"yQLM5kLHqFdrhfVd","rings":{"air":2,"earth":1,"fire":3,"water":2,"void":2},"skills":{"artisan":{"aesthetics":0,"composition":1,"design":0,"smithing":0},"martial":{"fitness":0,"melee":0,"ranged":0,"unarmed":0,"meditation":1,"tactics":1},"scholar":{"culture":0,"government":2,"medicine":0,"sentiment":1,"theology":1},"social":{"command":1,"courtesy":2,"games":0,"performance":1},"trade":{"commerce":0,"labor":0,"seafaring":0,"skulduggery":2,"survival":0}},"social":{"honor":30,"glory":40,"status":27,"ninjo":"Kogo yearns for power that cannot be taken away by political whims or clan hierarchies. Deep down, she wants to transcend the petty limitations of clan politics entirely - to become something more than a samurai bound by duty and status.","giri":"Her lord is Nasu Tadaaki, her own father and current head of the declining Nasu family. Her duty is to restore the family's status and influence with the Imperial families. Kogo must prove the Nasu worthy of their former position.","bushido_tenets":{"paramount":" Duty and Loyalty","less_significant":"Compassion"}},"derived":{"endurance":8,"composure":6,"focus":5,"vigilance":2,"void_points":2},"money":{"zeni":0,"koku":0,"bu":0},"advancements":[{"label":"Courtesy +1 (1 -> 2)","type":"skill","skill":"courtesy","ring":"void","at_rank":1,"xp":4,"in_curriculum":true},{"label":"Government +1 (1 -> 2)","type":"skill","skill":"government","ring":"void","at_rank":1,"xp":4,"in_curriculum":true}],"techniques":[{"name":"Prey on the Weak","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"shuji","rank":2,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Court is not a kind place, and a harsh word is no less cruel for being spoken softly and with perfect etiquette.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">As a Scheme action, you may make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">TN 1 Courtesy (air) check </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">targeting a Compromised character.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, your target must choose one of the following:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">- Immediately unmask in a manner of their choosing based on the circumstances.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">- Forfeit glory equal to your Air Ring plus your bonus successes to leave the scene.</span></p></li></ul><h4><span class=\"fontstyle5\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(air)</span><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle7\">+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If the target chooses to unmask, you learn one of their disadvantages of their choice per (op) spent this way.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(air)</span><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle7\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If the target chooses to leave the scene, you notice their destination from the direction of their departure or overhear from the crowd where they will retreat.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":215},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-shuji-l5r-sortilege.Item.ekziVajOr3Up1EjP","skill":"courtesy"},{"name":"Commune with the Spirits","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"ritual","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>The ritualist centers their mind on one of the Elements, appealing to the spirits in their environment and seeking their counsel or boon. Priests and laypeople are able to use this ritual to receive less specific guidance from the spirits, such as a leaf that falls to the ground pointing in the direction of the person or thing they are seeking.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">As a downtime activity or Support action, you may make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">TN 1 Theology check </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">using (air), (earth), (fire), (water), or (void) to appeal to nearby spirits of that Element (appeal to the departed, such as ancestor spirits, and other non-elemental supernatural presences, if using (void)) for aid.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, choose and receive one of the following boons from the spirit or spirits you contacted:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- Sense the Kami: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Detect all spirits and uses of their magic by shugenja within a number of range bands equal to the ring you used plus your bonus successes.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- Spiritual Knowledge: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Learn one fact the spirits know about the area.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- Elemental Gift: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">The kami deliver a small amount of the Element in question to you. For instance, a prayer to a water kami might cause it to begin raining lightly, for a short time, but it might also cause you to run across a stream, or even find groundwater. In contrast, a prayer to fire kami might bring forth a small shower of sparks, while a prayer to an air kami might elicit a gust of wind. Praying to an earth kami might cause you to stumble across a large stone, or find a small patch of arable ground amid a wasteland. Prayers to the ancestors may allow the petitioner to find something that belonged to an ancestor in a time of need.</span></p></li></ul><h4><span class=\"fontstyle5\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Reduce the TN of your next check to interact with or appeal to kami or supernatural presences of this Element by 1.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, receive one additional boon per </span><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op) </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">spent this way. Each boon can only be received one time per activation.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":212},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-rituals-l5r-sortilege.Item.r9DyFb62vtLwexbW","skill":"theology"},{"name":"By the Light of the Lord Moon","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"invocation","rank":1,"description":"<p>Kitsuki's Eyes (Ancestral), Wind Scatters Shadow (Elemental), Reveal the World of Ghosts (Foreign)</p><p><em>When a shugenja performs this invocation, the light shifts to that of a moonlit night, unweaving the shadows to lay bare the things they conceal. Hidden objects glow faintly with silver light, while mystical illusions are revealed as translucent, gossamer forms.</em></p><p><strong>Activation:</strong> As a Scheme action, you may make a TN 2 Theology (air) check targeting an area at range 0–2 of you.</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> If you succeed, you scry for each hidden character and concealed object (such as secret compartments, trap doors, and concealed weapons) in the targeted area, revealing it with an illusory, luminous outline that only you can perceive. This invocation only reveals objects and people concealed by mundane means.</p><h4>New Opportunities</h4><p>(air)(op)+: If you succeed, you may also reveal up to one magically concealed object per (op) spent this way.</p><p>Air(op)(op)+: Choose one additional character at range 0–1 per (op)(op) spent this way. The chosen characters can also see the objects.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":192},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-invocations-l5r-sortilege.Item.X37l2OFmdoUXYJtX","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Cloak of Night","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"invocation","rank":1,"description":"<p>Smoke of Stolen Light (Alchemy), Shroud of the North Wind (Fortunist), Walk in the Shadow World (Foreign)</p><p><em>A sufficiently learned shugenja can call forth air kami to play one of their simplest and most effective tricks: enveloping an object or person in their embrace to hide it from sight.</em></p><p><strong>Activation:</strong> As a Scheme and Support action, you may make a Theology (air) check targeting one object or character at range 0–1. The TN is equal to the target’s silhouette (see page 265).</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> If you succeed, you augment the target with an illusion that renders it invisible to the naked eye. The object is still physically present and can be touched, smelled, or sensed with any normal sense other than vision. This effect persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to your bonus successes.</p><h4>New Opportunities</h4><p>(air)(op)(op)+: Choose one additional target of the same silhouette or smaller per (op)(op) spent this way.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":192},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-invocations-l5r-sortilege.Item.fveOrp1xJ9uGnNCl","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Fukurokujin’s Wit","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"invocation","rank":1,"description":"<p>Wisdom of the Kitsu (Ancestral), Ignite the Mind's Candle (Elemental), Mantra of the Scholar Kings (Foreign)</p><p><em>Shujenja are scholars at their heart, for their art is one of long hours of study and dedication to the refinement of the mind. Thus, many seek the blessing of Fukurokujin, keeper of knowledge and patron to scholars. A shugenja can call upon the guidance of this Fortune to sharpen their mind to a razor edge and vitalize their nerves.</em></p><p><strong>Activation:</strong> As a Support action, you may make a TN 1 Theology (fire) check targeting yourself.</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> If you succeed, you augment your target’s wits and cunning with the Fortune’s favor. When making checks, the target adds a kept (ring) set to an (op)(st) result. This effect persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to your bonus successes.</p><h4>New Opportunities</h4><p>(fire)(op): You may target another character at range 0–2 instead of yourself.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":203},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-invocations-l5r-sortilege.Item.bH76OcZ5FOcuLRXx","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Sudden Nightfall","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":0,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"school_ability","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">You do not suffer any ill effects of Obscuring terrain as a result of darkness (see page 267 of the core rulebook). When you perform an Attack or Scheme action check against a target in terrain that is Obscuring due to darkness, reduce the TN by your school rank (to a minimum of 1).</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">As a Support action, you may target a position at range 0–2 and </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">summon </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">a cloud of supernatural darkness there. An area around the target position extending a number of range bands equal to your Air Ring become Obscuring terrain. This effect persists a number of rounds equal to your school rank.</span></p>","source":{"book":"celestial_realms","page":87},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.school-abilities-l5r-sortilege.Item.a06K6G42WcqlCnxQ"},{"name":"Deadly Sting","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":true,"bought_at_rank":1,"kind":"ninjutsu","rank":2,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Poison is not a weapon an honorable samurai would choose, but it is tremendously effective, and like its namesake, the Scorpion Clan is not above envenoming its weapons to defeat foes it otherwise could not best.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">As an Attack action, you may use one dose of a poison and make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">TN 3 Martial Arts (air) check </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">using a readied Concealable weapon targeting one character within the weapon’s range.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle4\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, apply the chosen poison to your weapon (see page 244). Then, the target suffers physical damage equal to the deadliness of your weapon plus your bonus successes.</span></p><h4><span class=\"fontstyle5\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(air)(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Move 1 range band.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(air)(op)+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, the target suffers a critical strike with severity 2, plus 1 per (op) spent this way.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":226},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-ninjitsu-l5r-sortilege.Item.9dRKaiSTJ9xnIdPK","skill":"melee,ranged,unarmed"},{"name":"Skulk","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":true,"bought_at_rank":1,"kind":"ninjutsu","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Shinobi are known for walking silently from shadow to shadow, moving like phantoms. Some of this relies upon agility and speed, of course, but veterans in the art of stealth know that using a crowd or another visual distraction to walk unnoticed can be as effective as the most complex acrobatics.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">When you perform an Initiative or Attack check using Air, you may spend (op) as follows:</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle4\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you are in Obscuring terrain, a crowd, or otherwise concealed from sight, one character with vigilance lower than or equal to your ranks in Skulduggery loses sight of you.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":226},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-ninjitsu-l5r-sortilege.Item.tKw2dMxzwVBuWOaT"},{"name":"Courtier’s Resolve","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":true,"bought_at_rank":1,"kind":"shuji","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Warriors do battle with their bodies, and courtiers do battle with their minds. To maintain one’s composure while surrounded by the challenges of court, one must be able to clear and organize one’s mind, returning focus to the most vital tasks.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Once per scene as a Support action, you may spend 1 Void point to recover from strife.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Remove strife equal to your glory rank.</span> <br style=\" font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: -webkit-auto; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; \"></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":222},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-shuji-l5r-sortilege.Item.KaIqecu4b1TpXZid"},{"name":"Sensational Distraction","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":true,"bought_at_rank":1,"kind":"shuji","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Standing out in court requires a great deal of both cunning and flair, and standing out on purpose can be even harder. Courtiers train for much of their lives to learn to control the perceptions of others at court. The best courtiers know when to draw attention to themselves with a display of rhetorical prowess or another social feat and when to avoid attention. Drawing attention to oneself can give collaborators the chance to work unnoticed as well, and thus it is an extremely valuable tool in the courtier’s arsenal.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">When making a Social skill (fire) check targeting one or more characters, you may spend (op) in the following way:</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle4\">(fire)(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">When interacting with other characters, the target treats their vigilance as 1 lower per (op) spent this way; when interacting with you, the target treats their vigilance as 1 higher per (op) spent this way. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":219},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-shuji-l5r-sortilege.Item.hYa08wHoU69Xu0GX"}],"peculiarities":[{"name":"Blackmail on Akodo Nobuhiko","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"distinction","ring":"fire","types":"Interpersonal","custom":true,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>“I had hoped to find you here,” Yogo Hiroue began. “It has been too long since we last spoke plainly.”</em></span></p><p></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">The following apply to a character with the Blackmail on [Name] distinction:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">- You have incriminating information on an individual, which you use to force them to help you even when doing so may damage their reputation. They will share what knowledge they have about a given person, item, location, or situation, whether through a face-to-face meeting or through written correspondence. They will also arrange for introductions with exclusive members of society or places of business. Confer with the GM to select a campaign-appropriate NPC when choosing this advantage.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">- When performing a check to demand favors of the chosen individual (such as a Courtesy (fire) check to remind them of the consequences of their disobeying you or a Command (fire) check to order them to risk themself on your behalf), you may reroll up to two dice.</span></p></li></ul>","source_reference":{"source":"core_rulebook","page":102}},{"name":"Tea","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"passion","ring":"void","types":"Physical, Spiritual","description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>“Without the bastions of civility that are teahouses, the Empire would surely collapse into chaos.”</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><em>– Kakita Yoshi, Daimyō of the Kakita Family</em></span></p><p></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">The following apply to a character with the Tea passion:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- You can identify regional variations in tea, and you know a great deal about the process of preparing and drying leaves. In the wilderness, you can acquire the natural ingredients required to make rustic teas of various sorts with relative ease.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- After performing a check to interact with tea (such as a Medicine (void) check to brew a tea with ingredients that help the body recover from illness or a Performance (void) check to perform a tea ceremony that helps the recipients contemplate their state in life), you remove 3 strife.</span></p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":115},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.passions-l5r-sortilege.Item.wiz5rooMR3tqtULe"},{"name":"Shadowlands Taint (Air)","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"adversity","ring":"air","types":"Curse, Interpersonal, Spiritual","description":"<p><em>The Obsidian Journal is a secret text, written hundreds  of years ago by Kuni Shunsuke, a Crab Clan samurai who made forbidden journeys into the Shadowlands  and wrote of what he saw there.</em></p><p><em>By the end of his journal, he wrote: “Even now, I know that the fingers of shadow have reached too deeply within me, for although I am surrounded by family and clan, I feel no kinship. They seem distant to me, as if viewed through a glass. I wonder how much of myself is truly left.”</em></p><p><em>That was the final entry of the Obsidian Journal. Kuni Shunsuke committed seppuku to silence the call of the Shadowlands.</em></p><p></p><p>The following apply to a character with the Shadowlands Taint (Air) adversity:</p><ul><li><p>-  You are a Tainted being. You have trouble sympathizing with other humans, but you can understand the emotions of corrupted beings easily.</p></li><li><p>-  When you make a check to show compassion for other human beings (such as a Composition (air) check to edit a work for emotional refinement or a Courtesy (air) check to say something difficult without harming the recipient’s feelings), you must choose and reroll two dice containing (su) or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point.</p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":127},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.adversities-l5r-sortilege.Item.eEg9b6rmnSBA5HqG"},{"name":"Conspiracy","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"anxiety","ring":"earth","types":"Interpersonal, Mental","description":"<p><em>“Why is she never seen out during the day?”</em></p><p><em>“Genjirō, you know the family keeps Lady Kaguya out of the sun because she burns so easily.”</em></p><p><em>“No, it’s because she feeds off the light of the moon.”</em></p><p><em>His friend sighed. “Moon people don’t exist, you know.”</em></p><p><em>“They do! They eat the dreams of their lovers, causing terrible nightmares.”</em></p><p><em>“Wait, does she eat dreams or moonlight?”</em></p><p><em>“You aren’t listening! If our lady’s bride-to-be isn’t human, we have to warn her. Now, moon people have a crescent-shaped birthmark on their—”</em></p><p><em>“We are not sneaking into Lady Kaguya’s bedroom to search her body! Do you want your head chopped off?”</em></p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> The following apply to a character with the Conspiracy anxiety:</p><ul><li><p>- You are plagued by the knowledge that there are greater plots in the world than what most others can see. Everywhere, treacherous schemes wait to ruin the lives of good people, and you cannot help but warn others of these awful machinations.</p></li><li><p>- After performing a check to interact with an unfamiliar authority figure (such as a Courtesy (earth) check to be properly deferential or a Government (earth) check to remember an authority figure’s specific role), you receive 3 strife. If this is the first time this has occurred this scene, gain 1 Void point.</p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"celestial_realms","page":91},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.anxieties-l5r-sortilege.Item.wBeHgMqK2BL7fX6I"},{"name":"Disdain for Compassion","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"adversity","ring":"water","types":"Flaw, Mental","description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>“We Brothers of the Boar are very loyal samurai, indeed! Loyal to money, loyal to our bellies, loyal to ourselves, and what higher virtue could there be, brothers, eh?”</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><em>- The Rōnin Kujira</em></span></p><p></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">The following apply to a character with the Disdain for Compassion adversity:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- You no longer believe in the tenet of Compassion, though you still lose honor for disobeying it. When you act in accordance with this tenet of Bushidō, others can sometimes sense your insincerity.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- When you make a check to pay lip service to this tenet of Bushidō or to uphold it (such as a Courtesy check to express its importance or a Meditation check to use a belief in this tenet to your advantage), you must choose and reroll two dice containing </span><span class=\"fontstyle5\">(su) </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point.</span></p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":120},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.adversities-l5r-sortilege.Item.WLiIHkS6o7pS2u9y"},{"name":"Benten’s Curse","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"adversity","ring":"air","types":"Interpersonal, Spiritual","description":"<p><em>One of the more popular tales of the rakugoka, the professional storytellers of Rokugan, is that of the Artless Artist. A comedic tale, it is the story of a court artist who was utterly lacking in any genuine talent and had such an unpleasant demeanor that nobody would ever love him. The telling of the tale varies from performance to performance, with the rakugoka spinning unique and outrageous recountings of the artist’s misadventures tailored to the tastes of their particular audience.</em></p><p></p><p>The following apply to a character with the Benten’s Curse adversity:</p><ul><li><p>- Your romantic efforts are always stymied by circumstances, and your gestures to get the romantic attention of others are usually misinterpreted.</p></li><li><p>- When you make a check to express your admiration to someone (such as an Aesthetics (air) check to find the right poem to read to express your feelings or a Courtesy (air) check to tell someone your feelings without exceeding propriety), you must choose and reroll two dice containing (su) or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point.</p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":116},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.adversities-l5r-sortilege.Item.wx0TwgTwrxGMVd1g"}],"titles":[],"bonds":[],"gear":[{"name":"Wakizashi","quantity":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Whereas the katana represents a samurai’s status as a warrior, the wakizashi represents their place in Rokugan’s social order and strict caste system. The wakizashi is a small, katana-like sword usually two to three feet in length, with the same flexible blade and lethal edge. It is often made as part of a pair, with the same decorations as its matched katana. The wakizashi also fills another role: it clearly signals that its wearer is a samurai, and a person of honor who will make the ultimate sacrifice for their ideals and their master. It is the tool with which a samurai commits seppuku: ritual suicide, the last protest of an aggrieved and honorable samurai.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":233},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.weapons-l5r-sortilege.Item.S1MG4qPHEV3N8XnO","damage":3,"deadliness":5,"range":"0-1","grip_2":"Deadliness +2","skill":"melee","category":"Swords","rarity":"7","zeni":"15 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000002","name":"Ceremonial"},{"id":"L5RCorePro000001","name":"Razor-Edged"}]},{"name":"Shuriken","quantity":6,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Favored by shinobi, shuriken are small metal discs with a sharpened edge that come in a dizzying array of sizes and styles. They are designed mainly to distract, but shuriken can also be coated with toxins for lethality, and any cutting edge can kill if used properly.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":237},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.weapons-l5r-sortilege.Item.5Lr1CNs1uvX7J38y","damage":2,"deadliness":4,"range":"0","grip_1":"(stab or slash): -, (thrown): Martial Arts [Ranged], Range 1-3","grip_2":"N/A","skill":"unarmed","category":"Specialist Weapons","rarity":"6","zeni":"1 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000005","name":"Concealable"}]},{"name":"Concealed Armor","quantity":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Used by cautious courtiers, shinobi, and anyone else who fears assassination, concealed armor is a kimono, keikogi, or other garment with thin bamboo or metal plates sewn inside to turn an unexpected blade or arrow.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":239},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.armors-l5r-sortilege.Item.vDEAuVf0o5GwmVsB","armor":{"physical":2,"supernatural":0},"rarity":"4","zeni":"5 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000005","name":"Concealable"}]},{"name":"Sanctified Robes","quantity":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">The vestments of shugenja, shrine keepers, and other religious figures are blessed by kami and thus grant mystical protection. Traditionally, such robes consist of a white garment called </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">jōe </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">(literally, “pure cloth”) and a peaked hat, but they can be simpler, such as a white haori top and red hakama bottoms, or even an elaborate kimono.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":239},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.armors-l5r-sortilege.Item.Cq1koK56k9dvLfMh","armor":{"physical":1,"supernatural":3},"rarity":"7","zeni":"4 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000002","name":"Ceremonial"}]},{"name":"Poison (One Vial)","quantity":3,"description":"<p>In the courts of the Emerald Empire, the wheels of politics are sometimes turned by unsavory means. Members of the Scorpion Clan are certainly not above using poison to weaken or eliminate political rivals—not that one could ever prove their culpability—and many samurai turn to such measures in times of desperation or fear. (Cost: 30 zeni for one dose. Rarity: 5. Qualities: Forbidden.)</p><p data-start=\"482\" data-end=\"1061\">Three poisons found in Rokugan are:<br data-start=\"517\" data-end=\"520\">$ Noxious Poison: A catchall term for a wide variety of deadly compounds (many of which have perfectly legitimate uses in medicine and other trades), these sorts of poisons often act by attacking the heart, organs, or brain directly.<br data-start=\"753\" data-end=\"756\">– When a character ingests noxious poison, the character suffers a critical strike with severity 10. The poisoner may spend  on their check to deliver the poison to increase the severity by 1 per  spent this way.<br data-start=\"970\" data-end=\"973\">– When noxious poison is applied to a weapon, increase that weapon’s deadliness by +4.</p><p data-start=\"1063\" data-end=\"1509\">$ Fire Biter: A poison that wracks victims with searing pain, fire biter is easily identified by its bitter taste, which makes it difficult to disguise its presence in food or drink.<br data-start=\"1245\" data-end=\"1248\">– When a character ingests fire biter, the character suffers 5 strife and the Dazed and Exhausted conditions.<br data-start=\"1357\" data-end=\"1360\">– When fire biter is applied to a weapon, after a target suffers a critical strike from the weapon, they suffer the Dazed and Exhausted conditions.</p><p data-start=\"1511\" data-end=\"1962\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">$ Night Milk: A favorite of the Shosuro family, night milk is a dizzying concoction that must be injected or otherwise delivered directly into the bloodstream.<br data-start=\"1670\" data-end=\"1673\">– When night milk is introduced into a character’s bloodstream, the character suffers 5 fatigue and the Disoriented and Prone conditions.<br data-start=\"1810\" data-end=\"1813\">– When night milk is applied to a weapon, after a target suffers a critical strike from the weapon, they suffer the Disoriented and Prone conditions.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":244},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.SNTCLZ2aScPEddId","rarity":"5","zeni":"30 zeni","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000009","name":"Forbidden"}]},{"name":"Tetsubishi","quantity":1,"description":"<p>A type of caltrop welded together in the shape of sharp-spined stars the size of a fist or larger, tetsubishi are a type of iron makibishi designed to be scattered on the battlefield in front of fortifications as a defense. They may also be used to delay pursuers. While their sharp edges may pierce the soles of unsuspecting samurai’s boots, these mass-produced weapons are especially effective at penetrating the hooves of horses used by cavalry and mounted infantry.</p><p data-start=\"473\" data-end=\"732\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">As an Attack and Support action, a character may scatter a handful of tetsubishi targeting a patch of ground at range 0–2. The terrain at range 0–1 from the point of impact gains the Dangerous and Ensnaring terrain quality. (Cost: 5 bu per handful. Rarity: 4)</p>","source":{"book":"fields_of_victory","page":91},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.4OCDJyLlEF5F7feH","rarity":"4","zeni":"5 bu"},{"name":"Calligraphy Set","quantity":1,"description":"<p>These ornate boxes contain items a practiced calligrapher needs to craft books, letters, scrolls, and other written communications. It consists of a small wooden box that contains a variety of brushes, inkstones, and pigments; a small bowl for water; and a small bag of sand for drying. Calligraphers and scribes customarily carry a calligraphy set, as so do some samurai and courtiers who prefer to write their own correspondence. (Cost: 1 bu. Rarity: 3.)</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":242},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.MWzx5Wiu6xcCWc9J","rarity":"3","zeni":"1 bu"},{"name":"Personal Seal or Chop","quantity":1,"description":"<p>A personal chop is used by samurai to verify their identity and sign documents, among other official business. Each one is a unique design that is registered with the Miya family. Using another samurai’s chop is considered both an insult and a serious crime. (Cost: 4 bu. Rarity: 6. Qualities: Ceremonial.)</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":243},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.UU5eQKPBQZ9ilOTF","rarity":"6","zeni":"4 bu","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000002","name":"Ceremonial"}]}]},{"xp":33,"label":"Interpreter, Rank 2","rank":2,"school":"Shosuro Shadowweaver School","foundry_id":"JVNV6v1nBOODVBs9","rings":{"air":2,"earth":1,"fire":3,"water":2,"void":2},"skills":{"artisan":{"aesthetics":0,"composition":2,"design":0,"smithing":0},"martial":{"fitness":0,"melee":0,"ranged":0,"unarmed":0,"meditation":1,"tactics":1},"scholar":{"culture":0,"government":3,"medicine":0,"sentiment":1,"theology":1},"social":{"command":1,"courtesy":2,"games":0,"performance":2},"trade":{"commerce":0,"labor":0,"seafaring":0,"skulduggery":2,"survival":0}},"social":{"honor":30,"glory":45,"status":32,"ninjo":"Kogo yearns for power that cannot be taken away by political whims or clan hierarchies. Deep down, she wants to transcend the petty limitations of clan politics entirely - to become something more than a samurai bound by duty and status.","giri":"Her lord is Nasu Tadaaki, her own father and current head of the declining Nasu family. Her duty is to restore the family's status and influence with the Imperial families. Kogo must prove the Nasu worthy of their former position.","bushido_tenets":{"paramount":" Duty and Loyalty","less_significant":"Compassion"}},"derived":{"endurance":8,"composure":6,"focus":5,"vigilance":2,"void_points":2},"money":{"zeni":0,"koku":0,"bu":0},"advancements":[{"label":"Courtesy +1 (1 -> 2)","type":"skill","skill":"courtesy","ring":"void","at_rank":1,"xp":4,"in_curriculum":true},{"label":"Government +1 (1 -> 2)","type":"skill","skill":"government","ring":"void","at_rank":1,"xp":4,"in_curriculum":true}],"techniques":[{"name":"Prey on the Weak","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"shuji","rank":2,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Court is not a kind place, and a harsh word is no less cruel for being spoken softly and with perfect etiquette.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">As a Scheme action, you may make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">TN 1 Courtesy (air) check </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">targeting a Compromised character.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, your target must choose one of the following:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">- Immediately unmask in a manner of their choosing based on the circumstances.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">- Forfeit glory equal to your Air Ring plus your bonus successes to leave the scene.</span></p></li></ul><h4><span class=\"fontstyle5\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(air)</span><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle7\">+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If the target chooses to unmask, you learn one of their disadvantages of their choice per (op) spent this way.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(air)</span><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle7\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If the target chooses to leave the scene, you notice their destination from the direction of their departure or overhear from the crowd where they will retreat.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":215},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-shuji-l5r-sortilege.Item.ekziVajOr3Up1EjP","skill":"courtesy"},{"name":"Commune with the Spirits","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"ritual","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>The ritualist centers their mind on one of the Elements, appealing to the spirits in their environment and seeking their counsel or boon. Priests and laypeople are able to use this ritual to receive less specific guidance from the spirits, such as a leaf that falls to the ground pointing in the direction of the person or thing they are seeking.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">As a downtime activity or Support action, you may make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">TN 1 Theology check </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">using (air), (earth), (fire), (water), or (void) to appeal to nearby spirits of that Element (appeal to the departed, such as ancestor spirits, and other non-elemental supernatural presences, if using (void)) for aid.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, choose and receive one of the following boons from the spirit or spirits you contacted:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- Sense the Kami: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Detect all spirits and uses of their magic by shugenja within a number of range bands equal to the ring you used plus your bonus successes.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- Spiritual Knowledge: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Learn one fact the spirits know about the area.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- Elemental Gift: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">The kami deliver a small amount of the Element in question to you. For instance, a prayer to a water kami might cause it to begin raining lightly, for a short time, but it might also cause you to run across a stream, or even find groundwater. In contrast, a prayer to fire kami might bring forth a small shower of sparks, while a prayer to an air kami might elicit a gust of wind. Praying to an earth kami might cause you to stumble across a large stone, or find a small patch of arable ground amid a wasteland. Prayers to the ancestors may allow the petitioner to find something that belonged to an ancestor in a time of need.</span></p></li></ul><h4><span class=\"fontstyle5\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Reduce the TN of your next check to interact with or appeal to kami or supernatural presences of this Element by 1.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, receive one additional boon per </span><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op) </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">spent this way. Each boon can only be received one time per activation.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":212},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-rituals-l5r-sortilege.Item.r9DyFb62vtLwexbW","skill":"theology"},{"name":"By the Light of the Lord Moon","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"invocation","rank":1,"description":"<p>Kitsuki's Eyes (Ancestral), Wind Scatters Shadow (Elemental), Reveal the World of Ghosts (Foreign)</p><p><em>When a shugenja performs this invocation, the light shifts to that of a moonlit night, unweaving the shadows to lay bare the things they conceal. Hidden objects glow faintly with silver light, while mystical illusions are revealed as translucent, gossamer forms.</em></p><p><strong>Activation:</strong> As a Scheme action, you may make a TN 2 Theology (air) check targeting an area at range 0–2 of you.</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> If you succeed, you scry for each hidden character and concealed object (such as secret compartments, trap doors, and concealed weapons) in the targeted area, revealing it with an illusory, luminous outline that only you can perceive. This invocation only reveals objects and people concealed by mundane means.</p><h4>New Opportunities</h4><p>(air)(op)+: If you succeed, you may also reveal up to one magically concealed object per (op) spent this way.</p><p>Air(op)(op)+: Choose one additional character at range 0–1 per (op)(op) spent this way. The chosen characters can also see the objects.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":192},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-invocations-l5r-sortilege.Item.X37l2OFmdoUXYJtX","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Cloak of Night","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"invocation","rank":1,"description":"<p>Smoke of Stolen Light (Alchemy), Shroud of the North Wind (Fortunist), Walk in the Shadow World (Foreign)</p><p><em>A sufficiently learned shugenja can call forth air kami to play one of their simplest and most effective tricks: enveloping an object or person in their embrace to hide it from sight.</em></p><p><strong>Activation:</strong> As a Scheme and Support action, you may make a Theology (air) check targeting one object or character at range 0–1. The TN is equal to the target’s silhouette (see page 265).</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> If you succeed, you augment the target with an illusion that renders it invisible to the naked eye. The object is still physically present and can be touched, smelled, or sensed with any normal sense other than vision. This effect persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to your bonus successes.</p><h4>New Opportunities</h4><p>(air)(op)(op)+: Choose one additional target of the same silhouette or smaller per (op)(op) spent this way.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":192},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-invocations-l5r-sortilege.Item.fveOrp1xJ9uGnNCl","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Fukurokujin’s Wit","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"invocation","rank":1,"description":"<p>Wisdom of the Kitsu (Ancestral), Ignite the Mind's Candle (Elemental), Mantra of the Scholar Kings (Foreign)</p><p><em>Shujenja are scholars at their heart, for their art is one of long hours of study and dedication to the refinement of the mind. Thus, many seek the blessing of Fukurokujin, keeper of knowledge and patron to scholars. A shugenja can call upon the guidance of this Fortune to sharpen their mind to a razor edge and vitalize their nerves.</em></p><p><strong>Activation:</strong> As a Support action, you may make a TN 1 Theology (fire) check targeting yourself.</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> If you succeed, you augment your target’s wits and cunning with the Fortune’s favor. When making checks, the target adds a kept (ring) set to an (op)(st) result. This effect persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to your bonus successes.</p><h4>New Opportunities</h4><p>(fire)(op): You may target another character at range 0–2 instead of yourself.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":203},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-invocations-l5r-sortilege.Item.bH76OcZ5FOcuLRXx","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Sudden Nightfall","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":0,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"school_ability","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">You do not suffer any ill effects of Obscuring terrain as a result of darkness (see page 267 of the core rulebook). When you perform an Attack or Scheme action check against a target in terrain that is Obscuring due to darkness, reduce the TN by your school rank (to a minimum of 1).</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">As a Support action, you may target a position at range 0–2 and </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">summon </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">a cloud of supernatural darkness there. An area around the target position extending a number of range bands equal to your Air Ring become Obscuring terrain. This effect persists a number of rounds equal to your school rank.</span></p>","source":{"book":"celestial_realms","page":87},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.school-abilities-l5r-sortilege.Item.a06K6G42WcqlCnxQ"},{"name":"Deadly Sting","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":true,"bought_at_rank":1,"kind":"ninjutsu","rank":2,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Poison is not a weapon an honorable samurai would choose, but it is tremendously effective, and like its namesake, the Scorpion Clan is not above envenoming its weapons to defeat foes it otherwise could not best.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">As an Attack action, you may use one dose of a poison and make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">TN 3 Martial Arts (air) check </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">using a readied Concealable weapon targeting one character within the weapon’s range.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle4\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, apply the chosen poison to your weapon (see page 244). Then, the target suffers physical damage equal to the deadliness of your weapon plus your bonus successes.</span></p><h4><span class=\"fontstyle5\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(air)(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Move 1 range band.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(air)(op)+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, the target suffers a critical strike with severity 2, plus 1 per (op) spent this way.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":226},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-ninjitsu-l5r-sortilege.Item.9dRKaiSTJ9xnIdPK","skill":"melee,ranged,unarmed"},{"name":"Skulk","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":true,"bought_at_rank":1,"kind":"ninjutsu","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Shinobi are known for walking silently from shadow to shadow, moving like phantoms. Some of this relies upon agility and speed, of course, but veterans in the art of stealth know that using a crowd or another visual distraction to walk unnoticed can be as effective as the most complex acrobatics.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">When you perform an Initiative or Attack check using Air, you may spend (op) as follows:</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle4\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you are in Obscuring terrain, a crowd, or otherwise concealed from sight, one character with vigilance lower than or equal to your ranks in Skulduggery loses sight of you.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":226},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-ninjitsu-l5r-sortilege.Item.tKw2dMxzwVBuWOaT"},{"name":"Courtier’s Resolve","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":true,"bought_at_rank":1,"kind":"shuji","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Warriors do battle with their bodies, and courtiers do battle with their minds. To maintain one’s composure while surrounded by the challenges of court, one must be able to clear and organize one’s mind, returning focus to the most vital tasks.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Once per scene as a Support action, you may spend 1 Void point to recover from strife.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Remove strife equal to your glory rank.</span> <br style=\" font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: -webkit-auto; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; \"></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":222},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-shuji-l5r-sortilege.Item.KaIqecu4b1TpXZid"},{"name":"Sensational Distraction","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":true,"bought_at_rank":1,"kind":"shuji","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Standing out in court requires a great deal of both cunning and flair, and standing out on purpose can be even harder. Courtiers train for much of their lives to learn to control the perceptions of others at court. The best courtiers know when to draw attention to themselves with a display of rhetorical prowess or another social feat and when to avoid attention. Drawing attention to oneself can give collaborators the chance to work unnoticed as well, and thus it is an extremely valuable tool in the courtier’s arsenal.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">When making a Social skill (fire) check targeting one or more characters, you may spend (op) in the following way:</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle4\">(fire)(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">When interacting with other characters, the target treats their vigilance as 1 lower per (op) spent this way; when interacting with you, the target treats their vigilance as 1 higher per (op) spent this way. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":219},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-shuji-l5r-sortilege.Item.hYa08wHoU69Xu0GX"},{"name":"Linguistic Liason","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":2,"kind":"title_ability","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">You learn the languages (written, spoken, signed, and any other forms, as relevant) of the group for which you are an interpreter. Additionally, the first time you make a check to interact socially with a member of this group each encounter, reduce the TN by 1.</span></p>","source":{"book":null,"page":0},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.title-abilities-l5r-sortilege.Item.QF5rWgOXVmHcXt8G"}],"peculiarities":[{"name":"Blackmail on Akodo Nobuhiko","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"distinction","ring":"fire","types":"Interpersonal","custom":true,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>“I had hoped to find you here,” Yogo Hiroue began. “It has been too long since we last spoke plainly.”</em></span></p><p></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">The following apply to a character with the Blackmail on [Name] distinction:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">- You have incriminating information on an individual, which you use to force them to help you even when doing so may damage their reputation. They will share what knowledge they have about a given person, item, location, or situation, whether through a face-to-face meeting or through written correspondence. They will also arrange for introductions with exclusive members of society or places of business. Confer with the GM to select a campaign-appropriate NPC when choosing this advantage.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">- When performing a check to demand favors of the chosen individual (such as a Courtesy (fire) check to remind them of the consequences of their disobeying you or a Command (fire) check to order them to risk themself on your behalf), you may reroll up to two dice.</span></p></li></ul>","source_reference":{"source":"core_rulebook","page":102}},{"name":"Tea","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"passion","ring":"void","types":"Physical, Spiritual","description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>“Without the bastions of civility that are teahouses, the Empire would surely collapse into chaos.”</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><em>– Kakita Yoshi, Daimyō of the Kakita Family</em></span></p><p></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">The following apply to a character with the Tea passion:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- You can identify regional variations in tea, and you know a great deal about the process of preparing and drying leaves. In the wilderness, you can acquire the natural ingredients required to make rustic teas of various sorts with relative ease.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- After performing a check to interact with tea (such as a Medicine (void) check to brew a tea with ingredients that help the body recover from illness or a Performance (void) check to perform a tea ceremony that helps the recipients contemplate their state in life), you remove 3 strife.</span></p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":115},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.passions-l5r-sortilege.Item.wiz5rooMR3tqtULe"},{"name":"Shadowlands Taint (Air)","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"adversity","ring":"air","types":"Curse, Interpersonal, Spiritual","description":"<p><em>The Obsidian Journal is a secret text, written hundreds  of years ago by Kuni Shunsuke, a Crab Clan samurai who made forbidden journeys into the Shadowlands  and wrote of what he saw there.</em></p><p><em>By the end of his journal, he wrote: “Even now, I know that the fingers of shadow have reached too deeply within me, for although I am surrounded by family and clan, I feel no kinship. They seem distant to me, as if viewed through a glass. I wonder how much of myself is truly left.”</em></p><p><em>That was the final entry of the Obsidian Journal. Kuni Shunsuke committed seppuku to silence the call of the Shadowlands.</em></p><p></p><p>The following apply to a character with the Shadowlands Taint (Air) adversity:</p><ul><li><p>-  You are a Tainted being. You have trouble sympathizing with other humans, but you can understand the emotions of corrupted beings easily.</p></li><li><p>-  When you make a check to show compassion for other human beings (such as a Composition (air) check to edit a work for emotional refinement or a Courtesy (air) check to say something difficult without harming the recipient’s feelings), you must choose and reroll two dice containing (su) or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point.</p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":127},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.adversities-l5r-sortilege.Item.eEg9b6rmnSBA5HqG"},{"name":"Conspiracy","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"anxiety","ring":"earth","types":"Interpersonal, Mental","description":"<p><em>“Why is she never seen out during the day?”</em></p><p><em>“Genjirō, you know the family keeps Lady Kaguya out of the sun because she burns so easily.”</em></p><p><em>“No, it’s because she feeds off the light of the moon.”</em></p><p><em>His friend sighed. “Moon people don’t exist, you know.”</em></p><p><em>“They do! They eat the dreams of their lovers, causing terrible nightmares.”</em></p><p><em>“Wait, does she eat dreams or moonlight?”</em></p><p><em>“You aren’t listening! If our lady’s bride-to-be isn’t human, we have to warn her. Now, moon people have a crescent-shaped birthmark on their—”</em></p><p><em>“We are not sneaking into Lady Kaguya’s bedroom to search her body! Do you want your head chopped off?”</em></p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> The following apply to a character with the Conspiracy anxiety:</p><ul><li><p>- You are plagued by the knowledge that there are greater plots in the world than what most others can see. Everywhere, treacherous schemes wait to ruin the lives of good people, and you cannot help but warn others of these awful machinations.</p></li><li><p>- After performing a check to interact with an unfamiliar authority figure (such as a Courtesy (earth) check to be properly deferential or a Government (earth) check to remember an authority figure’s specific role), you receive 3 strife. If this is the first time this has occurred this scene, gain 1 Void point.</p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"celestial_realms","page":91},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.anxieties-l5r-sortilege.Item.wBeHgMqK2BL7fX6I"},{"name":"Disdain for Compassion","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"adversity","ring":"water","types":"Flaw, Mental","description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>“We Brothers of the Boar are very loyal samurai, indeed! Loyal to money, loyal to our bellies, loyal to ourselves, and what higher virtue could there be, brothers, eh?”</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><em>- The Rōnin Kujira</em></span></p><p></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">The following apply to a character with the Disdain for Compassion adversity:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- You no longer believe in the tenet of Compassion, though you still lose honor for disobeying it. When you act in accordance with this tenet of Bushidō, others can sometimes sense your insincerity.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- When you make a check to pay lip service to this tenet of Bushidō or to uphold it (such as a Courtesy check to express its importance or a Meditation check to use a belief in this tenet to your advantage), you must choose and reroll two dice containing </span><span class=\"fontstyle5\">(su) </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point.</span></p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":120},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.adversities-l5r-sortilege.Item.WLiIHkS6o7pS2u9y"},{"name":"Benten’s Curse","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"adversity","ring":"air","types":"Interpersonal, Spiritual","description":"<p><em>One of the more popular tales of the rakugoka, the professional storytellers of Rokugan, is that of the Artless Artist. A comedic tale, it is the story of a court artist who was utterly lacking in any genuine talent and had such an unpleasant demeanor that nobody would ever love him. The telling of the tale varies from performance to performance, with the rakugoka spinning unique and outrageous recountings of the artist’s misadventures tailored to the tastes of their particular audience.</em></p><p></p><p>The following apply to a character with the Benten’s Curse adversity:</p><ul><li><p>- Your romantic efforts are always stymied by circumstances, and your gestures to get the romantic attention of others are usually misinterpreted.</p></li><li><p>- When you make a check to express your admiration to someone (such as an Aesthetics (air) check to find the right poem to read to express your feelings or a Courtesy (air) check to tell someone your feelings without exceeding propriety), you must choose and reroll two dice containing (su) or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point.</p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":116},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.adversities-l5r-sortilege.Item.wx0TwgTwrxGMVd1g"}],"titles":[{"name":"Interpreter (Ivory Kingdoms)","xp_used":13,"xp_cost":12,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":2,"custom":true,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Although many within Rokugan live their entire lives without thinking of the Empire’s neighbors, the truth is that many other civilizations touch upon the Emerald Empire in one way or another. Some, such as the Ivory Kingdoms, have contact by way of the shared danger that is the Shadowlands. Others, such as the Seikitsu of the northern mountains, exist much nearer geographically to Rokugan but are deeply distinct in culture and way of life. And as human cultures have different languages and customs, interpreters are often required to assist in situations where these groups interact.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Interpreters are expected to become fluent not only in the languages of the people they study but also in the practices and cultural touchstones of those groups. They must be able not only to translate but also to transliterate, understanding and conveying intent beyond the literal meaning of the words. This makes becoming an excellent interpreter a challenging process, requiring not only language skills but also keen insight into human nature.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Assigned By:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">The GM, after a character has gained an initial familiarity with another culture and desires to learn more.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Status Award:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">+5</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Glory Award:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">+5</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Special:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">A character who has completed this title can be assigned it again for a new group. The new instance of the title counts as a different title, which can be completed again, conferring benefits for the new group selected.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Title Ability:</strong> Linguistic Liaison</span></p><h2>Curriculum</h2><table><tbody><tr><td><p>Social Skills</p></td><td><p>Skill Group</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Composition</p></td><td><p>Skill</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Culture</p></td><td><p>Skill</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Government</p></td><td><p>Skill</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"compendium-link\" data-pack=\"l5r5e.core-techniques-shuji\">(shuji) Rank 1 Shuji</a> (prereq)</p></td><td><p>Tech. Grp.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"entity-link content-link\" draggable=\"true\" data-link=\"\" data-uuid=\"Compendium.l5r5e.core-techniques-rituals.Item.L5RCoreRit000037\" data-pack=\"l5r5e.core-techniques-rituals\" data-type=\"Item\" data-id=\"L5RCoreRit000037\">(ritual) Cultural Exchange</a> (prereq)</p></td><td><p>Technique</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"entity-link content-link\" draggable=\"true\" data-link=\"\" data-uuid=\"Compendium.l5r5e.core-techniques-rituals.Item.L5RCoreRit000041\" data-pack=\"l5r5e.core-techniques-rituals\" data-type=\"Item\" data-id=\"L5RCoreRit000041\">(ritual) Traveler's Experience</a> (prereq)</p></td><td><p>Technique</p></td></tr></tbody></table>","source_reference":{"source":"children_of_the_five_winds","page":135}}],"bonds":[],"gear":[{"name":"Wakizashi","quantity":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Whereas the katana represents a samurai’s status as a warrior, the wakizashi represents their place in Rokugan’s social order and strict caste system. The wakizashi is a small, katana-like sword usually two to three feet in length, with the same flexible blade and lethal edge. It is often made as part of a pair, with the same decorations as its matched katana. The wakizashi also fills another role: it clearly signals that its wearer is a samurai, and a person of honor who will make the ultimate sacrifice for their ideals and their master. It is the tool with which a samurai commits seppuku: ritual suicide, the last protest of an aggrieved and honorable samurai.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":233},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.weapons-l5r-sortilege.Item.S1MG4qPHEV3N8XnO","damage":3,"deadliness":5,"range":"0-1","grip_2":"Deadliness +2","skill":"melee","category":"Swords","rarity":"7","zeni":"15 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000002","name":"Ceremonial"},{"id":"L5RCorePro000001","name":"Razor-Edged"}]},{"name":"Shuriken","quantity":6,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Favored by shinobi, shuriken are small metal discs with a sharpened edge that come in a dizzying array of sizes and styles. They are designed mainly to distract, but shuriken can also be coated with toxins for lethality, and any cutting edge can kill if used properly.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":237},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.weapons-l5r-sortilege.Item.5Lr1CNs1uvX7J38y","damage":2,"deadliness":4,"range":"0","grip_1":"(stab or slash): -, (thrown): Martial Arts [Ranged], Range 1-3","grip_2":"N/A","skill":"unarmed","category":"Specialist Weapons","rarity":"6","zeni":"1 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000005","name":"Concealable"}]},{"name":"Concealed Armor","quantity":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Used by cautious courtiers, shinobi, and anyone else who fears assassination, concealed armor is a kimono, keikogi, or other garment with thin bamboo or metal plates sewn inside to turn an unexpected blade or arrow.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":239},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.armors-l5r-sortilege.Item.vDEAuVf0o5GwmVsB","armor":{"physical":2,"supernatural":0},"rarity":"4","zeni":"5 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000005","name":"Concealable"}]},{"name":"Sanctified Robes","quantity":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">The vestments of shugenja, shrine keepers, and other religious figures are blessed by kami and thus grant mystical protection. Traditionally, such robes consist of a white garment called </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">jōe </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">(literally, “pure cloth”) and a peaked hat, but they can be simpler, such as a white haori top and red hakama bottoms, or even an elaborate kimono.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":239},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.armors-l5r-sortilege.Item.Cq1koK56k9dvLfMh","armor":{"physical":1,"supernatural":3},"rarity":"7","zeni":"4 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000002","name":"Ceremonial"}]},{"name":"Poison (One Vial)","quantity":3,"description":"<p>In the courts of the Emerald Empire, the wheels of politics are sometimes turned by unsavory means. Members of the Scorpion Clan are certainly not above using poison to weaken or eliminate political rivals—not that one could ever prove their culpability—and many samurai turn to such measures in times of desperation or fear. (Cost: 30 zeni for one dose. Rarity: 5. Qualities: Forbidden.)</p><p data-start=\"482\" data-end=\"1061\">Three poisons found in Rokugan are:<br data-start=\"517\" data-end=\"520\">$ Noxious Poison: A catchall term for a wide variety of deadly compounds (many of which have perfectly legitimate uses in medicine and other trades), these sorts of poisons often act by attacking the heart, organs, or brain directly.<br data-start=\"753\" data-end=\"756\">– When a character ingests noxious poison, the character suffers a critical strike with severity 10. The poisoner may spend  on their check to deliver the poison to increase the severity by 1 per  spent this way.<br data-start=\"970\" data-end=\"973\">– When noxious poison is applied to a weapon, increase that weapon’s deadliness by +4.</p><p data-start=\"1063\" data-end=\"1509\">$ Fire Biter: A poison that wracks victims with searing pain, fire biter is easily identified by its bitter taste, which makes it difficult to disguise its presence in food or drink.<br data-start=\"1245\" data-end=\"1248\">– When a character ingests fire biter, the character suffers 5 strife and the Dazed and Exhausted conditions.<br data-start=\"1357\" data-end=\"1360\">– When fire biter is applied to a weapon, after a target suffers a critical strike from the weapon, they suffer the Dazed and Exhausted conditions.</p><p data-start=\"1511\" data-end=\"1962\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">$ Night Milk: A favorite of the Shosuro family, night milk is a dizzying concoction that must be injected or otherwise delivered directly into the bloodstream.<br data-start=\"1670\" data-end=\"1673\">– When night milk is introduced into a character’s bloodstream, the character suffers 5 fatigue and the Disoriented and Prone conditions.<br data-start=\"1810\" data-end=\"1813\">– When night milk is applied to a weapon, after a target suffers a critical strike from the weapon, they suffer the Disoriented and Prone conditions.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":244},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.SNTCLZ2aScPEddId","rarity":"5","zeni":"30 zeni","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000009","name":"Forbidden"}]},{"name":"Tetsubishi","quantity":1,"description":"<p>A type of caltrop welded together in the shape of sharp-spined stars the size of a fist or larger, tetsubishi are a type of iron makibishi designed to be scattered on the battlefield in front of fortifications as a defense. They may also be used to delay pursuers. While their sharp edges may pierce the soles of unsuspecting samurai’s boots, these mass-produced weapons are especially effective at penetrating the hooves of horses used by cavalry and mounted infantry.</p><p data-start=\"473\" data-end=\"732\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">As an Attack and Support action, a character may scatter a handful of tetsubishi targeting a patch of ground at range 0–2. The terrain at range 0–1 from the point of impact gains the Dangerous and Ensnaring terrain quality. (Cost: 5 bu per handful. Rarity: 4)</p>","source":{"book":"fields_of_victory","page":91},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.4OCDJyLlEF5F7feH","rarity":"4","zeni":"5 bu"},{"name":"Calligraphy Set","quantity":1,"description":"<p>These ornate boxes contain items a practiced calligrapher needs to craft books, letters, scrolls, and other written communications. It consists of a small wooden box that contains a variety of brushes, inkstones, and pigments; a small bowl for water; and a small bag of sand for drying. Calligraphers and scribes customarily carry a calligraphy set, as so do some samurai and courtiers who prefer to write their own correspondence. (Cost: 1 bu. Rarity: 3.)</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":242},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.MWzx5Wiu6xcCWc9J","rarity":"3","zeni":"1 bu"},{"name":"Personal Seal or Chop","quantity":1,"description":"<p>A personal chop is used by samurai to verify their identity and sign documents, among other official business. Each one is a unique design that is registered with the Miya family. Using another samurai’s chop is considered both an insult and a serious crime. (Cost: 4 bu. Rarity: 6. Qualities: Ceremonial.)</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":243},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.UU5eQKPBQZ9ilOTF","rarity":"6","zeni":"4 bu","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000002","name":"Ceremonial"}]}]},{"xp":63,"label":"Interpreter, Rank 3","rank":3,"school":"Shosuro Shadowweaver School","foundry_id":"HhUYx9efAco0z2SQ","rings":{"air":2,"earth":1,"fire":3,"water":2,"void":2},"skills":{"artisan":{"aesthetics":0,"composition":2,"design":0,"smithing":0},"martial":{"fitness":0,"melee":0,"ranged":2,"unarmed":0,"meditation":1,"tactics":1},"scholar":{"culture":0,"government":3,"medicine":0,"sentiment":1,"theology":1},"social":{"command":1,"courtesy":2,"games":0,"performance":2},"trade":{"commerce":0,"labor":0,"seafaring":0,"skulduggery":2,"survival":0}},"social":{"honor":30,"glory":45,"status":32,"ninjo":"Kogo yearns for power that cannot be taken away by political whims or clan hierarchies. Deep down, she wants to transcend the petty limitations of clan politics entirely - to become something more than a samurai bound by duty and status.","giri":"Her lord is Nasu Tadaaki, her own father and current head of the declining Nasu family. Her duty is to restore the family's status and influence with the Imperial families. Kogo must prove the Nasu worthy of their former position.","bushido_tenets":{"paramount":" Duty and Loyalty","less_significant":"Compassion"}},"derived":{"endurance":8,"composure":6,"focus":5,"vigilance":2,"void_points":2},"money":{"zeni":0,"koku":0,"bu":0},"advancements":[{"label":"Courtesy +1 (1 -> 2)","type":"skill","skill":"courtesy","ring":"void","at_rank":1,"xp":4,"in_curriculum":true},{"label":"Government +1 (1 -> 2)","type":"skill","skill":"government","ring":"void","at_rank":1,"xp":4,"in_curriculum":true},{"label":"Martial Arts [Ranged] +1 (0 -> 1)","type":"skill","skill":"ranged","ring":"void","at_rank":2,"xp":2,"in_curriculum":true},{"label":"Martial Arts [Ranged] +1 (1 -> 2)","type":"skill","skill":"ranged","ring":"void","at_rank":2,"xp":4,"in_curriculum":true}],"techniques":[{"name":"Prey on the Weak","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"shuji","rank":2,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Court is not a kind place, and a harsh word is no less cruel for being spoken softly and with perfect etiquette.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">As a Scheme action, you may make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">TN 1 Courtesy (air) check </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">targeting a Compromised character.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, your target must choose one of the following:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">- Immediately unmask in a manner of their choosing based on the circumstances.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">- Forfeit glory equal to your Air Ring plus your bonus successes to leave the scene.</span></p></li></ul><h4><span class=\"fontstyle5\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(air)</span><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle7\">+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If the target chooses to unmask, you learn one of their disadvantages of their choice per (op) spent this way.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(air)</span><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle7\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If the target chooses to leave the scene, you notice their destination from the direction of their departure or overhear from the crowd where they will retreat.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":215},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-shuji-l5r-sortilege.Item.ekziVajOr3Up1EjP","skill":"courtesy"},{"name":"Commune with the Spirits","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"ritual","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>The ritualist centers their mind on one of the Elements, appealing to the spirits in their environment and seeking their counsel or boon. Priests and laypeople are able to use this ritual to receive less specific guidance from the spirits, such as a leaf that falls to the ground pointing in the direction of the person or thing they are seeking.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">As a downtime activity or Support action, you may make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">TN 1 Theology check </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">using (air), (earth), (fire), (water), or (void) to appeal to nearby spirits of that Element (appeal to the departed, such as ancestor spirits, and other non-elemental supernatural presences, if using (void)) for aid.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, choose and receive one of the following boons from the spirit or spirits you contacted:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- Sense the Kami: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Detect all spirits and uses of their magic by shugenja within a number of range bands equal to the ring you used plus your bonus successes.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- Spiritual Knowledge: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Learn one fact the spirits know about the area.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- Elemental Gift: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">The kami deliver a small amount of the Element in question to you. For instance, a prayer to a water kami might cause it to begin raining lightly, for a short time, but it might also cause you to run across a stream, or even find groundwater. In contrast, a prayer to fire kami might bring forth a small shower of sparks, while a prayer to an air kami might elicit a gust of wind. Praying to an earth kami might cause you to stumble across a large stone, or find a small patch of arable ground amid a wasteland. Prayers to the ancestors may allow the petitioner to find something that belonged to an ancestor in a time of need.</span></p></li></ul><h4><span class=\"fontstyle5\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Reduce the TN of your next check to interact with or appeal to kami or supernatural presences of this Element by 1.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, receive one additional boon per </span><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op) </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">spent this way. Each boon can only be received one time per activation.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":212},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-rituals-l5r-sortilege.Item.r9DyFb62vtLwexbW","skill":"theology"},{"name":"By the Light of the Lord Moon","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"invocation","rank":1,"description":"<p>Kitsuki's Eyes (Ancestral), Wind Scatters Shadow (Elemental), Reveal the World of Ghosts (Foreign)</p><p><em>When a shugenja performs this invocation, the light shifts to that of a moonlit night, unweaving the shadows to lay bare the things they conceal. Hidden objects glow faintly with silver light, while mystical illusions are revealed as translucent, gossamer forms.</em></p><p><strong>Activation:</strong> As a Scheme action, you may make a TN 2 Theology (air) check targeting an area at range 0–2 of you.</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> If you succeed, you scry for each hidden character and concealed object (such as secret compartments, trap doors, and concealed weapons) in the targeted area, revealing it with an illusory, luminous outline that only you can perceive. This invocation only reveals objects and people concealed by mundane means.</p><h4>New Opportunities</h4><p>(air)(op)+: If you succeed, you may also reveal up to one magically concealed object per (op) spent this way.</p><p>Air(op)(op)+: Choose one additional character at range 0–1 per (op)(op) spent this way. The chosen characters can also see the objects.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":192},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-invocations-l5r-sortilege.Item.X37l2OFmdoUXYJtX","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Cloak of Night","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"invocation","rank":1,"description":"<p>Smoke of Stolen Light (Alchemy), Shroud of the North Wind (Fortunist), Walk in the Shadow World (Foreign)</p><p><em>A sufficiently learned shugenja can call forth air kami to play one of their simplest and most effective tricks: enveloping an object or person in their embrace to hide it from sight.</em></p><p><strong>Activation:</strong> As a Scheme and Support action, you may make a Theology (air) check targeting one object or character at range 0–1. The TN is equal to the target’s silhouette (see page 265).</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> If you succeed, you augment the target with an illusion that renders it invisible to the naked eye. The object is still physically present and can be touched, smelled, or sensed with any normal sense other than vision. This effect persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to your bonus successes.</p><h4>New Opportunities</h4><p>(air)(op)(op)+: Choose one additional target of the same silhouette or smaller per (op)(op) spent this way.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":192},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-invocations-l5r-sortilege.Item.fveOrp1xJ9uGnNCl","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Fukurokujin’s Wit","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"invocation","rank":1,"description":"<p>Wisdom of the Kitsu (Ancestral), Ignite the Mind's Candle (Elemental), Mantra of the Scholar Kings (Foreign)</p><p><em>Shujenja are scholars at their heart, for their art is one of long hours of study and dedication to the refinement of the mind. Thus, many seek the blessing of Fukurokujin, keeper of knowledge and patron to scholars. A shugenja can call upon the guidance of this Fortune to sharpen their mind to a razor edge and vitalize their nerves.</em></p><p><strong>Activation:</strong> As a Support action, you may make a TN 1 Theology (fire) check targeting yourself.</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> If you succeed, you augment your target’s wits and cunning with the Fortune’s favor. When making checks, the target adds a kept (ring) set to an (op)(st) result. This effect persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to your bonus successes.</p><h4>New Opportunities</h4><p>(fire)(op): You may target another character at range 0–2 instead of yourself.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":203},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-invocations-l5r-sortilege.Item.bH76OcZ5FOcuLRXx","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Sudden Nightfall","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":0,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"school_ability","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">You do not suffer any ill effects of Obscuring terrain as a result of darkness (see page 267 of the core rulebook). When you perform an Attack or Scheme action check against a target in terrain that is Obscuring due to darkness, reduce the TN by your school rank (to a minimum of 1).</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">As a Support action, you may target a position at range 0–2 and </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">summon </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">a cloud of supernatural darkness there. An area around the target position extending a number of range bands equal to your Air Ring become Obscuring terrain. This effect persists a number of rounds equal to your school rank.</span></p>","source":{"book":"celestial_realms","page":87},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.school-abilities-l5r-sortilege.Item.a06K6G42WcqlCnxQ"},{"name":"Deadly Sting","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":true,"bought_at_rank":1,"kind":"ninjutsu","rank":2,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Poison is not a weapon an honorable samurai would choose, but it is tremendously effective, and like its namesake, the Scorpion Clan is not above envenoming its weapons to defeat foes it otherwise could not best.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">As an Attack action, you may use one dose of a poison and make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">TN 3 Martial Arts (air) check </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">using a readied Concealable weapon targeting one character within the weapon’s range.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle4\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, apply the chosen poison to your weapon (see page 244). Then, the target suffers physical damage equal to the deadliness of your weapon plus your bonus successes.</span></p><h4><span class=\"fontstyle5\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(air)(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Move 1 range band.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(air)(op)+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, the target suffers a critical strike with severity 2, plus 1 per (op) spent this way.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":226},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-ninjitsu-l5r-sortilege.Item.9dRKaiSTJ9xnIdPK","skill":"melee,ranged,unarmed"},{"name":"Skulk","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":true,"bought_at_rank":1,"kind":"ninjutsu","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Shinobi are known for walking silently from shadow to shadow, moving like phantoms. Some of this relies upon agility and speed, of course, but veterans in the art of stealth know that using a crowd or another visual distraction to walk unnoticed can be as effective as the most complex acrobatics.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">When you perform an Initiative or Attack check using Air, you may spend (op) as follows:</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle4\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you are in Obscuring terrain, a crowd, or otherwise concealed from sight, one character with vigilance lower than or equal to your ranks in Skulduggery loses sight of you.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":226},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-ninjitsu-l5r-sortilege.Item.tKw2dMxzwVBuWOaT"},{"name":"Courtier’s Resolve","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":true,"bought_at_rank":1,"kind":"shuji","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Warriors do battle with their bodies, and courtiers do battle with their minds. To maintain one’s composure while surrounded by the challenges of court, one must be able to clear and organize one’s mind, returning focus to the most vital tasks.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Once per scene as a Support action, you may spend 1 Void point to recover from strife.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Remove strife equal to your glory rank.</span> <br style=\" font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: -webkit-auto; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; \"></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":222},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-shuji-l5r-sortilege.Item.KaIqecu4b1TpXZid"},{"name":"Sensational Distraction","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":true,"bought_at_rank":1,"kind":"shuji","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Standing out in court requires a great deal of both cunning and flair, and standing out on purpose can be even harder. Courtiers train for much of their lives to learn to control the perceptions of others at court. The best courtiers know when to draw attention to themselves with a display of rhetorical prowess or another social feat and when to avoid attention. Drawing attention to oneself can give collaborators the chance to work unnoticed as well, and thus it is an extremely valuable tool in the courtier’s arsenal.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">When making a Social skill (fire) check targeting one or more characters, you may spend (op) in the following way:</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle4\">(fire)(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">When interacting with other characters, the target treats their vigilance as 1 lower per (op) spent this way; when interacting with you, the target treats their vigilance as 1 higher per (op) spent this way. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":219},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-shuji-l5r-sortilege.Item.hYa08wHoU69Xu0GX"},{"name":"Linguistic Liason","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":2,"kind":"title_ability","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">You learn the languages (written, spoken, signed, and any other forms, as relevant) of the group for which you are an interpreter. Additionally, the first time you make a check to interact socially with a member of this group each encounter, reduce the TN by 1.</span></p>","source":{"book":null,"page":0},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.title-abilities-l5r-sortilege.Item.QF5rWgOXVmHcXt8G"},{"name":"Commune with Evil","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":2,"kind":"maho","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>The practitioner detects any malevolent supernatural entities in the area, senses their desires, and makes a bargain for an unholy blessing.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">As a downtime activity action, you may make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">TN 1 Theology (void) check</span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, you </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">scry </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">for the presence of any Otherworldly or Tainted beings at range 0–6.</span></p><h4><span class=\"fontstyle0\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">(op): </span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">If there are any such beings, they accept your offering, and they </span><span class=\"fontstyle5\">augment </span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">you with an unholy blessing that increases the value of the ring you used for the check by 1. You can only have one unholy blessing at a time, and it persists until the end of the scene.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">(op)(op)(op)+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">If you receive an unholy blessing, it temporarily increases the ring’s value by an additional 1 per </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(op)(op)(op) </span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">spent this way.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">(op)+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">If you receive an unholy blessing, it persists for 1 additional round per (op) spent this way.</span></p>","source":{"book":"shadowlands","page":118},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-maho-l5r-sortilege.Item.XXHWw0ydoD5ktFR3","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Incite Haunting","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":2,"kind":"maho","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>Kansen are kami twisted by the power of Fu Leng, and they need little prompting to cause harm. Directing them toward a target with a vile rite and profane words that seem to warp the air, the mahō-tsukai afflicts a poor soul with a spiritual malady that can fester and bloom, fueling darker curses still. Spiritualists can perceive kansen as wretched, ghostly figures, clinging to their victim and dragging them inexorably toward a wretched end wrought by their worst nature.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">As an Attack and Scheme action, you may make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Theology check </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">targeting one character at range 0–1. This check uses any ring of your choice, and the TN of the check is equal to the target’s vigilance.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, you </span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">curse </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">your target, causing them to suffer the Afflicted condition. If you fail, the target rebuffs your efforts. If your shortfall is 2 or higher, the target also becomes aware of your attempted malediction.</span></p><h4><span class=\"fontstyle5\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Treat the maximum range of the technique as 1 higher per (op) spent this way.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(op)+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Choose one additional target per (op) spent this way.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":224},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-maho-l5r-sortilege.Item.GsIvHMI0O2s07ypl","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Sinful Whispers","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":2,"kind":"maho","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">The kansen assail the victim’s mind, murmuring dark things that slowly erode their concentration, making them more receptive to the words of the mahō-tsukai and less able to think coherently.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">As an Attack and Scheme action, you may make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Theology (air) check </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">targeting one character with the Afflicted condition at range 0–4. The TN of the check is equal to the target’s vigilance.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, you </span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">curse </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">your target, sapping their will; they must answer your questions honestly (and find doing so unremarkable at the time). This effect persists for a number of rounds equal to your Air Ring.</span></p><h4><span class=\"fontstyle5\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(air)(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">The target does not remember what you asked, even if prompted to think about the conversation later.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(air)(op)(op)(op): </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">You may give the target a single simple order. The target may ignore that order, but receives 2 strife at the end of each scene in which they disregard it. When the target becomes Compromised, they must unmask and attempt to fulfill the order until the end of the scene.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":225},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-maho-l5r-sortilege.Item.Wlqbwh2FX0QpEUDU","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Unholy Fervor","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":2,"kind":"maho","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>The kansen bite and tear the flesh of the victim, wracking them with pain that transforms into mindless fury.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">As a Support action, you may make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Theology (Fire) check </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">targeting one character at range 0–3. The TN of this check is equal to the target’s vigilance.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, you </span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">curse </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">the target with blinding fury; they suffer the Enraged condition. If you succeed, you </span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">augment </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">the target's corruption; they may treat each of their Shadowlands Taint disadvantages as an advantage that apply to any checks using its ring. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</span></p><h4><span class=\"fontstyle5\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle6\">(fire)(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">: Each target receives strife equal to your Fire Ring and removes that much fatigue.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(fire)(op)+: </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Choose one additional target per</span><span class=\"fontstyle6\"></span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">spent this way.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":225},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-maho-l5r-sortilege.Item.Y36kLAUCpuiSxSD7","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Accursed Summoning","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":2,"kind":"maho","rank":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><em>The mahō-tsukai spills blood and recites a foul prayer to summon a chosen oni and bind it to their will. The oni appears caught in an invisible prison, unable to act except at the summoner’s direction.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">As a downtime activity action, you may make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Theology (void) check </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">with TN equal to the oni’s Intrigue rank.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">If you succeed, you </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">summon </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">the desired oni and </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">bind </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">it to your will, unable to act without your consent. If you fail, you </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">summon </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">the desired oni (or a different one, at the GM’s discretion) but it breaks free of your control and curses you, causing you to suffer the Afflicted condition. If you have 3 or more kept (st) results, the summoned oni </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">scries </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">and learns your name.</span></p><h4><span class=\"fontstyle5\">New Opportunities:</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle4\">(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">+</span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">The sight of the oni instills primal terror in any onlookers. Each character who can see the oni and is within range 3 suffers a number of strife equal to </span><span class=\"fontstyle4\">(op) </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">spent this way.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle4\">(op)(op)</span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">: </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">The oni instills a Shadowlands Taint disadvantage of your choice upon anyone within a range equal to the number of your rings with the Shadowlands Taint disadvantage attached.</span></p>","source":{"book":"shadowlands","page":118},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-maho-l5r-sortilege.Item.NFND9NcuM2omMQpD","skill":"theology"},{"name":"Lord Bayushi’s Whispers (Scorpion)","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":true,"bought_at_rank":2,"kind":"shuji","rank":2,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>The Kami Bayushi, self-appointed villain of the Emperor Hantei and master of duplicity, founded the Scorpion Clan with a simple purpose: to dishonor themselves so that others could live honorably. Bayushi maintained vast networks of spies and informants, and he was extremely skilled at turning assets others used to try to spy on him. The Scorpion Clan has carried on this tradition with an efficiency that would surely make Bayushi proud. Hardly a town exists in the Empire without an agent of the Scorpion.</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Activation:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Once per game session, during a narrative scene or as a downtime activity, you may make a </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">TN 2 Skulduggery (void) check </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">to uncover an informant who can give you information about a subject.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Effects:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, you reveal one informant who can give you information about a topic of your choice. If the informant’s profile is required, use an appropriate NPC of the GM’s choice (see </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Chapter 8: Non-Player Characters</span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">).</span></p><h4><span class=\"fontstyle4\">New Opportunities</span></h4><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">(void)(op): </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">If you succeed, choose one skill. The informant has a number of ranks in that skill equal to your school rank and can perform checks with that skill to assist you until the end of the scene.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":223},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-shuji-l5r-sortilege.Item.zsXZtTrofBlj3FYg","skill":"skulduggery"},{"name":"Fluid Shadows","xp_used":3,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":true,"bought_at_rank":2,"kind":"invocation","rank":2,"description":"<p>Nekoma’s Silent Prowl (Ancestral), One With the Spirit’s River (Elemental), Communion of the Shadow Trees (Foreign)</p><p><em>When you become one with the shadows of a place, it is as if you were never there to begin with.</em></p><p><strong>Activation:</strong> As a Movement and Scheme action, you may make a TN 2 Theology (water) check targeting a shadowy position (such as Obscuring terrain) at range 1–3.</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> If you succeed, you summon yourself to that position instantly.</p><h4>New Opportunities</h4><p>(water)(op)+: Treat the maximum range of this technique as 1 higher per (op) spent this way.</p><p>(water)(op)(op): Increase the TN of Attack and Scheme action checks targeting you by 2 (instead of 1 from Attack actions from the effects of Obscuring terrain) until the end of your next turn.</p>","source":{"book":"celestial_realms","page":108},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.techniques-invocations-l5r-sortilege.Item.l05XM6wPSsXeLWhg","skill":"theology"}],"peculiarities":[{"name":"Blackmail on Akodo Nobuhiko","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"distinction","ring":"fire","types":"Interpersonal","custom":true,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>“I had hoped to find you here,” Yogo Hiroue began. “It has been too long since we last spoke plainly.”</em></span></p><p></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">The following apply to a character with the Blackmail on [Name] distinction:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle3\">- You have incriminating information on an individual, which you use to force them to help you even when doing so may damage their reputation. They will share what knowledge they have about a given person, item, location, or situation, whether through a face-to-face meeting or through written correspondence. They will also arrange for introductions with exclusive members of society or places of business. Confer with the GM to select a campaign-appropriate NPC when choosing this advantage.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">- When performing a check to demand favors of the chosen individual (such as a Courtesy (fire) check to remind them of the consequences of their disobeying you or a Command (fire) check to order them to risk themself on your behalf), you may reroll up to two dice.</span></p></li></ul>","source_reference":{"source":"core_rulebook","page":102}},{"name":"Tea","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"passion","ring":"void","types":"Physical, Spiritual","description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>“Without the bastions of civility that are teahouses, the Empire would surely collapse into chaos.”</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><em>– Kakita Yoshi, Daimyō of the Kakita Family</em></span></p><p></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">The following apply to a character with the Tea passion:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- You can identify regional variations in tea, and you know a great deal about the process of preparing and drying leaves. In the wilderness, you can acquire the natural ingredients required to make rustic teas of various sorts with relative ease.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- After performing a check to interact with tea (such as a Medicine (void) check to brew a tea with ingredients that help the body recover from illness or a Performance (void) check to perform a tea ceremony that helps the recipients contemplate their state in life), you remove 3 strife.</span></p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":115},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.passions-l5r-sortilege.Item.wiz5rooMR3tqtULe"},{"name":"Shadowlands Taint (Air)","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"adversity","ring":"air","types":"Curse, Interpersonal, Spiritual","description":"<p><em>The Obsidian Journal is a secret text, written hundreds  of years ago by Kuni Shunsuke, a Crab Clan samurai who made forbidden journeys into the Shadowlands  and wrote of what he saw there.</em></p><p><em>By the end of his journal, he wrote: “Even now, I know that the fingers of shadow have reached too deeply within me, for although I am surrounded by family and clan, I feel no kinship. They seem distant to me, as if viewed through a glass. I wonder how much of myself is truly left.”</em></p><p><em>That was the final entry of the Obsidian Journal. Kuni Shunsuke committed seppuku to silence the call of the Shadowlands.</em></p><p></p><p>The following apply to a character with the Shadowlands Taint (Air) adversity:</p><ul><li><p>-  You are a Tainted being. You have trouble sympathizing with other humans, but you can understand the emotions of corrupted beings easily.</p></li><li><p>-  When you make a check to show compassion for other human beings (such as a Composition (air) check to edit a work for emotional refinement or a Courtesy (air) check to say something difficult without harming the recipient’s feelings), you must choose and reroll two dice containing (su) or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point.</p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":127},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.adversities-l5r-sortilege.Item.eEg9b6rmnSBA5HqG"},{"name":"Conspiracy","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"anxiety","ring":"earth","types":"Interpersonal, Mental","description":"<p><em>“Why is she never seen out during the day?”</em></p><p><em>“Genjirō, you know the family keeps Lady Kaguya out of the sun because she burns so easily.”</em></p><p><em>“No, it’s because she feeds off the light of the moon.”</em></p><p><em>His friend sighed. “Moon people don’t exist, you know.”</em></p><p><em>“They do! They eat the dreams of their lovers, causing terrible nightmares.”</em></p><p><em>“Wait, does she eat dreams or moonlight?”</em></p><p><em>“You aren’t listening! If our lady’s bride-to-be isn’t human, we have to warn her. Now, moon people have a crescent-shaped birthmark on their—”</em></p><p><em>“We are not sneaking into Lady Kaguya’s bedroom to search her body! Do you want your head chopped off?”</em></p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> The following apply to a character with the Conspiracy anxiety:</p><ul><li><p>- You are plagued by the knowledge that there are greater plots in the world than what most others can see. Everywhere, treacherous schemes wait to ruin the lives of good people, and you cannot help but warn others of these awful machinations.</p></li><li><p>- After performing a check to interact with an unfamiliar authority figure (such as a Courtesy (earth) check to be properly deferential or a Government (earth) check to remember an authority figure’s specific role), you receive 3 strife. If this is the first time this has occurred this scene, gain 1 Void point.</p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"celestial_realms","page":91},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.anxieties-l5r-sortilege.Item.wBeHgMqK2BL7fX6I"},{"name":"Disdain for Compassion","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"adversity","ring":"water","types":"Flaw, Mental","description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em>“We Brothers of the Boar are very loyal samurai, indeed! Loyal to money, loyal to our bellies, loyal to ourselves, and what higher virtue could there be, brothers, eh?”</em></span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><em>- The Rōnin Kujira</em></span></p><p></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">The following apply to a character with the Disdain for Compassion adversity:</span></p><ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- You no longer believe in the tenet of Compassion, though you still lose honor for disobeying it. When you act in accordance with this tenet of Bushidō, others can sometimes sense your insincerity.</span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">- When you make a check to pay lip service to this tenet of Bushidō or to uphold it (such as a Courtesy check to express its importance or a Meditation check to use a belief in this tenet to your advantage), you must choose and reroll two dice containing </span><span class=\"fontstyle5\">(su) </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point.</span></p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":120},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.adversities-l5r-sortilege.Item.WLiIHkS6o7pS2u9y"},{"name":"Benten’s Curse","xp_used":0,"xp_cost":3,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":0,"kind":"adversity","ring":"air","types":"Interpersonal, Spiritual","description":"<p><em>One of the more popular tales of the rakugoka, the professional storytellers of Rokugan, is that of the Artless Artist. A comedic tale, it is the story of a court artist who was utterly lacking in any genuine talent and had such an unpleasant demeanor that nobody would ever love him. The telling of the tale varies from performance to performance, with the rakugoka spinning unique and outrageous recountings of the artist’s misadventures tailored to the tastes of their particular audience.</em></p><p></p><p>The following apply to a character with the Benten’s Curse adversity:</p><ul><li><p>- Your romantic efforts are always stymied by circumstances, and your gestures to get the romantic attention of others are usually misinterpreted.</p></li><li><p>- When you make a check to express your admiration to someone (such as an Aesthetics (air) check to find the right poem to read to express your feelings or a Courtesy (air) check to tell someone your feelings without exceeding propriety), you must choose and reroll two dice containing (su) or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point.</p></li></ul>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":116},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.adversities-l5r-sortilege.Item.wx0TwgTwrxGMVd1g"}],"titles":[{"name":"Interpreter (Ivory Kingdoms)","xp_used":13,"xp_cost":12,"in_curriculum":false,"bought_at_rank":2,"custom":true,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Although many within Rokugan live their entire lives without thinking of the Empire’s neighbors, the truth is that many other civilizations touch upon the Emerald Empire in one way or another. Some, such as the Ivory Kingdoms, have contact by way of the shared danger that is the Shadowlands. Others, such as the Seikitsu of the northern mountains, exist much nearer geographically to Rokugan but are deeply distinct in culture and way of life. And as human cultures have different languages and customs, interpreters are often required to assist in situations where these groups interact.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Interpreters are expected to become fluent not only in the languages of the people they study but also in the practices and cultural touchstones of those groups. They must be able not only to translate but also to transliterate, understanding and conveying intent beyond the literal meaning of the words. This makes becoming an excellent interpreter a challenging process, requiring not only language skills but also keen insight into human nature.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Assigned By:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">The GM, after a character has gained an initial familiarity with another culture and desires to learn more.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Status Award:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">+5</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Glory Award:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">+5</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Special:</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">A character who has completed this title can be assigned it again for a new group. The new instance of the title counts as a different title, which can be completed again, conferring benefits for the new group selected.</span></p><p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Title Ability:</strong> Linguistic Liaison</span></p><h2>Curriculum</h2><table><tbody><tr><td><p>Social Skills</p></td><td><p>Skill Group</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Composition</p></td><td><p>Skill</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Culture</p></td><td><p>Skill</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Government</p></td><td><p>Skill</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"compendium-link\" data-pack=\"l5r5e.core-techniques-shuji\">(shuji) Rank 1 Shuji</a> (prereq)</p></td><td><p>Tech. Grp.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"entity-link content-link\" draggable=\"true\" data-link=\"\" data-uuid=\"Compendium.l5r5e.core-techniques-rituals.Item.L5RCoreRit000037\" data-pack=\"l5r5e.core-techniques-rituals\" data-type=\"Item\" data-id=\"L5RCoreRit000037\">(ritual) Cultural Exchange</a> (prereq)</p></td><td><p>Technique</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><a class=\"entity-link content-link\" draggable=\"true\" data-link=\"\" data-uuid=\"Compendium.l5r5e.core-techniques-rituals.Item.L5RCoreRit000041\" data-pack=\"l5r5e.core-techniques-rituals\" data-type=\"Item\" data-id=\"L5RCoreRit000041\">(ritual) Traveler's Experience</a> (prereq)</p></td><td><p>Technique</p></td></tr></tbody></table>","source_reference":{"source":"children_of_the_five_winds","page":135}}],"bonds":[],"gear":[{"name":"Wakizashi","quantity":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Whereas the katana represents a samurai’s status as a warrior, the wakizashi represents their place in Rokugan’s social order and strict caste system. The wakizashi is a small, katana-like sword usually two to three feet in length, with the same flexible blade and lethal edge. It is often made as part of a pair, with the same decorations as its matched katana. The wakizashi also fills another role: it clearly signals that its wearer is a samurai, and a person of honor who will make the ultimate sacrifice for their ideals and their master. It is the tool with which a samurai commits seppuku: ritual suicide, the last protest of an aggrieved and honorable samurai.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":233},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.weapons-l5r-sortilege.Item.S1MG4qPHEV3N8XnO","damage":3,"deadliness":5,"range":"0-1","grip_2":"Deadliness +2","skill":"melee","category":"Swords","rarity":"7","zeni":"15 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000002","name":"Ceremonial"},{"id":"L5RCorePro000001","name":"Razor-Edged"}]},{"name":"Shuriken","quantity":6,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Favored by shinobi, shuriken are small metal discs with a sharpened edge that come in a dizzying array of sizes and styles. They are designed mainly to distract, but shuriken can also be coated with toxins for lethality, and any cutting edge can kill if used properly.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":237},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.weapons-l5r-sortilege.Item.5Lr1CNs1uvX7J38y","damage":2,"deadliness":4,"range":"0","grip_1":"(stab or slash): -, (thrown): Martial Arts [Ranged], Range 1-3","grip_2":"N/A","skill":"unarmed","category":"Specialist Weapons","rarity":"6","zeni":"1 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000005","name":"Concealable"}]},{"name":"Concealed Armor","quantity":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Used by cautious courtiers, shinobi, and anyone else who fears assassination, concealed armor is a kimono, keikogi, or other garment with thin bamboo or metal plates sewn inside to turn an unexpected blade or arrow.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":239},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.armors-l5r-sortilege.Item.vDEAuVf0o5GwmVsB","armor":{"physical":2,"supernatural":0},"rarity":"4","zeni":"5 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000005","name":"Concealable"}]},{"name":"Sanctified Robes","quantity":1,"description":"<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">The vestments of shugenja, shrine keepers, and other religious figures are blessed by kami and thus grant mystical protection. Traditionally, such robes consist of a white garment called </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">jōe </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">(literally, “pure cloth”) and a peaked hat, but they can be simpler, such as a white haori top and red hakama bottoms, or even an elaborate kimono.</span></p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":239},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.armors-l5r-sortilege.Item.Cq1koK56k9dvLfMh","armor":{"physical":1,"supernatural":3},"rarity":"7","zeni":"4 koku","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000002","name":"Ceremonial"}]},{"name":"Poison (One Vial)","quantity":3,"description":"<p>In the courts of the Emerald Empire, the wheels of politics are sometimes turned by unsavory means. Members of the Scorpion Clan are certainly not above using poison to weaken or eliminate political rivals—not that one could ever prove their culpability—and many samurai turn to such measures in times of desperation or fear. (Cost: 30 zeni for one dose. Rarity: 5. Qualities: Forbidden.)</p><p data-start=\"482\" data-end=\"1061\">Three poisons found in Rokugan are:<br data-start=\"517\" data-end=\"520\">$ Noxious Poison: A catchall term for a wide variety of deadly compounds (many of which have perfectly legitimate uses in medicine and other trades), these sorts of poisons often act by attacking the heart, organs, or brain directly.<br data-start=\"753\" data-end=\"756\">– When a character ingests noxious poison, the character suffers a critical strike with severity 10. The poisoner may spend  on their check to deliver the poison to increase the severity by 1 per  spent this way.<br data-start=\"970\" data-end=\"973\">– When noxious poison is applied to a weapon, increase that weapon’s deadliness by +4.</p><p data-start=\"1063\" data-end=\"1509\">$ Fire Biter: A poison that wracks victims with searing pain, fire biter is easily identified by its bitter taste, which makes it difficult to disguise its presence in food or drink.<br data-start=\"1245\" data-end=\"1248\">– When a character ingests fire biter, the character suffers 5 strife and the Dazed and Exhausted conditions.<br data-start=\"1357\" data-end=\"1360\">– When fire biter is applied to a weapon, after a target suffers a critical strike from the weapon, they suffer the Dazed and Exhausted conditions.</p><p data-start=\"1511\" data-end=\"1962\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">$ Night Milk: A favorite of the Shosuro family, night milk is a dizzying concoction that must be injected or otherwise delivered directly into the bloodstream.<br data-start=\"1670\" data-end=\"1673\">– When night milk is introduced into a character’s bloodstream, the character suffers 5 fatigue and the Disoriented and Prone conditions.<br data-start=\"1810\" data-end=\"1813\">– When night milk is applied to a weapon, after a target suffers a critical strike from the weapon, they suffer the Disoriented and Prone conditions.</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":244},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.SNTCLZ2aScPEddId","rarity":"5","zeni":"30 zeni","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000009","name":"Forbidden"}]},{"name":"Tetsubishi","quantity":1,"description":"<p>A type of caltrop welded together in the shape of sharp-spined stars the size of a fist or larger, tetsubishi are a type of iron makibishi designed to be scattered on the battlefield in front of fortifications as a defense. They may also be used to delay pursuers. While their sharp edges may pierce the soles of unsuspecting samurai’s boots, these mass-produced weapons are especially effective at penetrating the hooves of horses used by cavalry and mounted infantry.</p><p data-start=\"473\" data-end=\"732\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">As an Attack and Support action, a character may scatter a handful of tetsubishi targeting a patch of ground at range 0–2. The terrain at range 0–1 from the point of impact gains the Dangerous and Ensnaring terrain quality. (Cost: 5 bu per handful. Rarity: 4)</p>","source":{"book":"fields_of_victory","page":91},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.4OCDJyLlEF5F7feH","rarity":"4","zeni":"5 bu"},{"name":"Calligraphy Set","quantity":1,"description":"<p>These ornate boxes contain items a practiced calligrapher needs to craft books, letters, scrolls, and other written communications. It consists of a small wooden box that contains a variety of brushes, inkstones, and pigments; a small bowl for water; and a small bag of sand for drying. Calligraphers and scribes customarily carry a calligraphy set, as so do some samurai and courtiers who prefer to write their own correspondence. (Cost: 1 bu. Rarity: 3.)</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":242},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.MWzx5Wiu6xcCWc9J","rarity":"3","zeni":"1 bu"},{"name":"Personal Seal or Chop","quantity":1,"description":"<p>A personal chop is used by samurai to verify their identity and sign documents, among other official business. Each one is a unique design that is registered with the Miya family. Using another samurai’s chop is considered both an insult and a serious crime. (Cost: 4 bu. Rarity: 6. Qualities: Ceremonial.)</p>","source":{"book":"core_rulebook","page":243},"uuid":"Compendium.l5r5e-compendia-sortilege.items-l5r-sortilege.Item.UU5eQKPBQZ9ilOTF","rarity":"6","zeni":"4 bu","properties":[{"id":"L5RCorePro000002","name":"Ceremonial"}]}]}]};
